WEBVTT

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.153
[music: "My Bias, My Boss" theme song]

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:52.707
(This drama is a work of fiction)

00:00:52.731 --> 00:00:54.000
(Any similarity to real people, organizations, or events is coincidental)

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.122
[Hagi grunts] [intriguing music] (Hagi) Luni.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.710
If someone gives wine as a gift

00:00:57.777 --> 00:01:00.080
And says it's a gift from the heart, what does it mean?

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:03.767
Plus, I heard it's a wine known for making your love come true.

00:01:04.331 --> 00:01:05.265
[Luni whispering] Phrases like that are used

00:01:05.332 --> 00:01:06.633
When expressing

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:09.002
Their romantic interest.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.335
Romantic...

00:01:11.424 --> 00:01:12.339
Interest?

00:01:12.406 --> 00:01:15.542
(Luni) She must have feelings for you!

00:01:15.609 --> 00:01:16.701
[ding sound]

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:19.245
[music stops] [phone vibrating]

00:01:20.969 --> 00:01:22.269
(Chan)

00:01:29.723 --> 00:01:32.659
(Lee Chan) Dareum, I'll be away for a few days starting tomorrow.

00:01:32.883 --> 00:01:36.183
Can I see you for a moment before I go?

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:39.646
[lively music]

00:01:39.713 --> 00:01:40.701
(Hagi) She...

00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:43.070
Likes me?

00:01:49.571 --> 00:01:51.267
[footsteps approaching]

00:02:02.168 --> 00:02:03.290
[laughs]

00:02:08.014 --> 00:02:09.329
[laughs]

00:02:09.396 --> 00:02:10.631
[cat meowing sound]

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:13.233
[sparkling sound] [music fades]

00:02:17.884 --> 00:02:19.933
Let's go. I'll walk you home.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.592
(Dareum) It's okay.

00:02:21.659 --> 00:02:24.914
I have somewhere I need to stop by. I can go by myself.

00:02:24.981 --> 00:02:26.000
But...

00:02:26.506 --> 00:02:28.192
(Hagi) I should still walk you home...

00:02:28.259 --> 00:02:30.651
(Dareum) Mr. Kang, are you all right?

00:02:31.375 --> 00:02:32.819
Of course I am.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.872
Why wouldn't I be?

00:02:34.939 --> 00:02:36.767
You're acting a bit odd,

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:38.267
And your face is red...

00:02:39.026 --> 00:02:40.812
[intriguing music]

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:41.962
(Hagi) Just...

00:02:42.489 --> 00:02:43.797
Just go now. [comical sound]

00:02:43.864 --> 00:02:45.499
- (Dareum) What? - I take back my offer.

00:02:46.077 --> 00:02:46.866
I take it back!

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:49.434
(Hagi) Just go now. [Dareum exhales]

00:02:50.398 --> 00:02:51.269
(Dareum) Okay.

00:02:51.336 --> 00:02:54.000
I'll get going, then.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:00.247
[rustles]

00:03:00.848 --> 00:03:02.549
Bye.

00:03:02.616 --> 00:03:03.817
[door opens]

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:05.839
[music stops] [door closes]

00:03:05.906 --> 00:03:07.036
[door lock sound]

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:10.934
[Hagi sighs]

00:03:13.716 --> 00:03:15.759
This one is obviously heavier.

00:03:15.826 --> 00:03:17.638
They're not the same at all.

00:03:18.525 --> 00:03:20.973
Why does my mom seem to like Kang Hagi more than her own son?

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.002
[door closes]

00:03:22.069 --> 00:03:23.133
She's unbelievable.

00:03:24.741 --> 00:03:26.000
[intriguing music]

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:27.240
[creak sound]

00:03:31.454 --> 00:03:32.501
(Minwoo) What?

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:34.881
Why is a woman coming out of that house?

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:35.867
[door opens] [music stops]

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:37.083
(Minwoo) Who was that?

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.085
[door closes] Who is she?

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.320
(Episode 5) Why would an employee visit your house?

00:03:40.387 --> 00:03:42.100
And what's with those lovestruck eyes? [thuds]

00:03:42.923 --> 00:03:45.759
(Hagi) I had a proposal to fix urgently, so she came to help me. Okay?

00:03:45.826 --> 00:03:48.228
(Minwoo) But I feel like I've seen her somewhere...

00:03:48.295 --> 00:03:49.696
[intriguing music] [rustling]

00:03:49.763 --> 00:03:50.764
Right!

00:03:50.831 --> 00:03:52.198
The nosebleed! The ice! [ding sounds]

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:54.381
Right? The one who threw the drunken fit last time! [swish sound]

00:03:54.448 --> 00:03:55.969
Wow... [Minwoo laughs]

00:03:56.036 --> 00:03:58.105
And she's your employee now?

00:03:58.172 --> 00:03:59.873
(Hagi) Mind your own business.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.007
(Minwoo) What?

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:04.444
Wow, wine...

00:04:04.511 --> 00:04:07.233
So work was just an excuse. That was a date, wasn't it? [smacks]

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:10.333
I didn't prepare it. She bought it for me,

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.551
(Hagi) and said it was a gift from the heart.

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:13.987
(Minwoo) No way! Then she's the one who asked you out?

00:04:14.054 --> 00:04:15.756
[whoosh sound] [music stops]

00:04:18.425 --> 00:04:19.526
(Hagi) Well...

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:21.594
She didn't say it directly, but... [exciting music]

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:24.130
(Dareum) Mr. Kang, drink this [whoosh sound]

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.459
And cheer up.

00:04:25.526 --> 00:04:27.033
Hang in there! [whoosh sound]

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:29.233
[comical sound] (Hagi) I mean...

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.868
She walked up to me

00:04:31.657 --> 00:04:32.638
And told me to cheer up.

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.508
(Dareum) Mr. Kang! [whoosh sound]

00:04:36.349 --> 00:04:37.511
I'll sit next to you.

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.100
[grunts]

00:04:39.167 --> 00:04:41.200
(Hagi) She suddenly keeps touching me... [whoosh sound]

00:04:42.429 --> 00:04:43.783
Gosh...

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:44.784
And more than anything...

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.620
[heart beating sound] [laughs]

00:04:46.687 --> 00:04:48.830
[heartbeat growing faster]

00:04:49.698 --> 00:04:50.968
She smiles whenever she sees me.

00:04:51.877 --> 00:04:53.126
Wow...

00:04:53.594 --> 00:04:54.728
(Hagi) She must

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:56.930
Like me, right?

00:04:58.832 --> 00:05:00.400
No. [music stops]

00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:01.535
[Hagi grunts]

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:03.370
(Minwoo) Not just "like."

00:05:04.802 --> 00:05:05.594
It's "love."

00:05:05.661 --> 00:05:06.940
Love. [voice echoes] [heart beating sound]

00:05:07.007 --> 00:05:08.795
[passionate music] (Hagi) What?

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:11.377
Love?

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:12.279
[whoosh sound]

00:05:12.732 --> 00:05:13.613
[whoosh sound]

00:05:14.014 --> 00:05:14.915
Love.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:16.883
[sparkling sound]

00:05:17.551 --> 00:05:18.585
[whistling sound]

00:05:18.652 --> 00:05:19.699
Love.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.855
[footsteps fading] [music stops]

00:05:21.922 --> 00:05:23.264
[thuds] [Hagi reacts]

00:05:24.867 --> 00:05:26.579
[faint dog barking] [insects chirping]

00:05:29.403 --> 00:05:32.103
(Chan Can I see you for a moment before I go?)

00:05:32.633 --> 00:05:33.738
[notification ping]

00:05:34.762 --> 00:05:40.462
(Youverse Lee Chan started a livestream)

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:44.376
Hi. It's been a while, hasn't it? [emotional music]

00:05:45.715 --> 00:05:47.348
(Lee Chan on screen) I have to leave early tomorrow,

00:05:47.372 --> 00:05:48.667
So I can't talk long.

00:05:50.517 --> 00:05:51.484
I just...

00:05:51.985 --> 00:05:54.421
Wanted to see you all.

00:05:56.757 --> 00:06:00.100
I can't see your faces, but you can see me.

00:06:04.262 --> 00:06:06.233
I wanted to say something to you.

00:06:07.651 --> 00:06:09.035
I know I can be immature

00:06:09.636 --> 00:06:11.404
And hurt you sometimes,

00:06:12.439 --> 00:06:14.341
But thank you for always supporting me.

00:06:15.811 --> 00:06:17.944
I really mean it.

00:06:19.813 --> 00:06:20.973
[faint sigh]

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:23.770
[Lee Chan clears throat on screen]

00:06:24.918 --> 00:06:26.686
I read in one of my favorite books

00:06:27.354 --> 00:06:30.189
That in time, your sincerity will always come through.

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:34.327
So I hope my sincerity reaches you too.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.836
It's late.

00:06:42.903 --> 00:06:44.471
I should go to bed now.

00:06:46.196 --> 00:06:47.574
I'll come back next time. Bye.

00:06:50.033 --> 00:06:51.601
(The livestream has ended) [clicks] [beeps]

00:06:52.779 --> 00:06:54.340
[sighs] [phone vibrating]

00:07:01.788 --> 00:07:06.192
(Dareum) I don't have time today. I'll see you next time. [message notification sound]

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:06.994
[message notification sound]

00:07:07.018 --> 00:07:09.818
And you don't need to worry

00:07:09.842 --> 00:07:11.842
About what happened that day.

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:15.567
(Lee Chan) Thanks for messaging me back, Dareum. [message notification sound]

00:07:16.169 --> 00:07:18.038
[message notification sound] (Dareum) I hope the shoot goes well.

00:07:18.062 --> 00:07:19.549
I'll be rooting for you.

00:07:19.573 --> 00:07:20.707
[faint laugh]

00:07:21.875 --> 00:07:23.083
[insects chirping]

00:07:25.929 --> 00:07:26.980
[phone clacks]

00:07:27.714 --> 00:07:28.748
[sighs]

00:07:33.234 --> 00:07:34.394
[music stops]

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.591
[street sounds]

00:07:38.658 --> 00:07:40.360
[intriguing music]

00:07:40.427 --> 00:07:42.224
(Hagi) Get a grip, Kang Hagi!

00:07:42.291 --> 00:07:43.363
Just act...

00:07:45.195 --> 00:07:46.399
Like you normally do.

00:07:49.102 --> 00:07:50.070
[card reader beeps]

00:07:56.122 --> 00:07:57.077
[sighs]

00:07:59.501 --> 00:08:00.680
[music stops]

00:08:02.003 --> 00:08:03.416
[footsteps approaching]

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:05.151
[sparkling sound]

00:08:07.175 --> 00:08:08.154
(Hagi) Oh...

00:08:09.077 --> 00:08:10.867
Thank... [Dareum grunts] [cheerful music]

00:08:10.934 --> 00:08:12.434
[heart beating sound] you...

00:08:13.108 --> 00:08:14.011
Mr. Kang,

00:08:14.078 --> 00:08:15.944
(Dareum) did you find any more stickers at home?

00:08:16.011 --> 00:08:18.464
It was pretty fun yesterday. It was like a treasure hunt.

00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:20.593
- If you find any more... - Ms. Nam.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:21.902
(Dareum) Yes? [music stretches and stops]

00:08:21.969 --> 00:08:23.234
We're at work.

00:08:24.137 --> 00:08:24.962
[Dareum reacts]

00:08:25.029 --> 00:08:26.339
[whoosh sound] [intriguing music] I'm the CEO.

00:08:26.406 --> 00:08:27.622
(CEO) [thud sounds]

00:08:27.689 --> 00:08:29.142
[comical sound] (Hagi) And you're an employee.

00:08:29.209 --> 00:08:30.367
(Employee) [thud sounds]

00:08:31.186 --> 00:08:32.145
Let's... [whoosh sound]

00:08:32.876 --> 00:08:33.956
Keep things... [whoosh sound]

00:08:34.023 --> 00:08:34.867
Professional.

00:08:34.934 --> 00:08:36.383
[blinking sound]

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:37.453
[whoosh sound]

00:08:38.601 --> 00:08:39.786
[flaps]

00:08:41.388 --> 00:08:42.422
[whoosh sound]

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:45.602
[whoosh sound]

00:08:45.669 --> 00:08:46.626
[comical sound]

00:08:47.935 --> 00:08:49.329
[Dareum gasps] [Hagi huffs]

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:51.865
(Dareum) Oh, my gosh! [elevator dings]

00:08:51.932 --> 00:08:53.767
[music stops] [elevator doors opening]

00:08:56.069 --> 00:08:58.237
[buttons beeping] (automated voice) Doors... Doors... Doors closing.

00:08:58.304 --> 00:09:00.304
Mr. Kang! [cheerful music]

00:09:00.371 --> 00:09:02.709
(Dareum) Mr. Kang, let me... [banging]

00:09:04.711 --> 00:09:06.000
What?

00:09:07.067 --> 00:09:08.681
What's going on with him?

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.267
What did I do wrong this time? [music stops]

00:09:13.053 --> 00:09:14.409
[Jinsang clears throat]

00:09:14.476 --> 00:09:15.831
[employees murmuring]

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:17.626
[relief sound] [Jinsang clears throat]

00:09:17.693 --> 00:09:18.891
[Jinsang clears throat]

00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:21.061
Excuse me. Sorry. [Jinsang clears throat]

00:09:21.761 --> 00:09:23.610
I have to go out to the front when Mr. Kang calls me later,

00:09:23.677 --> 00:09:25.725
So give me some space.

00:09:25.792 --> 00:09:27.293
(Miyeong) You? Why?

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:28.717
(Jinsang) What do you mean, why?

00:09:28.784 --> 00:09:32.187
Look. "K-Wave project." It's worth 1.5 billion won.

00:09:32.254 --> 00:09:33.133
[Jinsang laughs]

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:34.941
- Want to take a look? - (Sungwook) Really?

00:09:35.008 --> 00:09:35.968
(Jinsang) Yeah.

00:09:36.492 --> 00:09:39.012
(Sungwook) "Dalgona-shaped keychain that has a sweet taste."

00:09:39.079 --> 00:09:40.947
Is this really all a grown-up can come up with?

00:09:41.014 --> 00:09:42.148
This is definitely getting rejected.

00:09:42.215 --> 00:09:43.216
(Jinsang) Hey!

00:09:43.283 --> 00:09:46.231
This is definitely going to attract bugs.

00:09:46.298 --> 00:09:47.227
- (Jinsang) What? - (Miyeong) Yeah.

00:09:47.294 --> 00:09:48.974
(Sungwook) I hope it goes well. [Miyeong reacts]

00:09:49.041 --> 00:09:51.224
- (Jinsang) That look... - (Hagi) Let's begin the meeting.

00:09:53.493 --> 00:09:54.575
[Jinsang grunts]

00:09:55.228 --> 00:09:56.600
[beeps] We held an internal competition

00:09:56.667 --> 00:09:59.831
To submit proposals for the K-Wave project organized by the Korea Heritage Service.

00:09:59.898 --> 00:10:01.921
(Hagi) I'll announce the winner today.

00:10:01.988 --> 00:10:03.896
[drumroll sound] Since there was only one spot

00:10:03.963 --> 00:10:07.817
For the fashion category, the item was the most important factor.

00:10:07.884 --> 00:10:09.042
The selected idea is...

00:10:09.109 --> 00:10:10.043
[laughs]

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:11.578
Lee...

00:10:12.133 --> 00:10:13.868
[Jinsang exclaims and exhales]

00:10:15.682 --> 00:10:16.705
[drumroll stops]

00:10:16.772 --> 00:10:18.751
[beeps] Mina's mosaic wrapping cloth.

00:10:19.385 --> 00:10:20.760
[employees gasp] (Dareum) Oh, my gosh!

00:10:20.827 --> 00:10:23.210
(Dareum, Yeongwoo) Wow! [employees clap]

00:10:23.277 --> 00:10:25.634
[bright music] [Dareum, Yeongwoo exclaim]

00:10:25.959 --> 00:10:27.060
- (Miyeong) Sit down. - (Sungwook) Sit down, dalgona.

00:10:27.127 --> 00:10:28.528
(Yeongwoo) Ms. Lee, congratulations!

00:10:29.805 --> 00:10:31.031
Amazing.

00:10:31.098 --> 00:10:32.732
(Hagi) Ms. Lee, why don't you come to the front and explain your idea?

00:10:33.257 --> 00:10:34.388
Okay!

00:10:34.455 --> 00:10:35.343
[Yeongwoo exclaims]

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:38.004
[Mina gasps] [employees cheer and clap]

00:10:38.071 --> 00:10:39.072
(Yeongwoo) You're so cool!

00:10:39.139 --> 00:10:40.634
[Jinsang claps loudly]

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:45.534
[Mina gasps] [music stops]

00:10:45.601 --> 00:10:48.348
[Mina exclaims] Hello.

00:10:48.415 --> 00:10:50.550
(Mina) I'm a new employee on the MD team,

00:10:50.617 --> 00:10:51.418
[off-pitch] Lee Mina...

00:10:51.485 --> 00:10:52.852
[bright music] [laughing]

00:10:52.919 --> 00:10:54.320
[employees laugh quietly]

00:10:54.387 --> 00:10:56.189
- Nice to meet you... - (Yeongwoo) She's nervous.

00:10:56.256 --> 00:10:57.869
[gasps]

00:10:57.936 --> 00:10:59.718
[beeps] Well...

00:10:59.785 --> 00:11:01.711
(Mina) The item I came up with

00:11:01.778 --> 00:11:03.062
Is a mosaic wrapping cloth,

00:11:03.129 --> 00:11:05.968
Inspired by traditional Korean patchwork.

00:11:06.035 --> 00:11:09.632
We'll be collaborating with a textile shop in Jongno

00:11:09.699 --> 00:11:12.772
That's been in business for three generations.

00:11:13.371 --> 00:11:14.367
[beeps]

00:11:14.434 --> 00:11:16.863
Since Korean patchwork

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:19.863
Is very similar to mosaics and stained glass,

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:23.513
I believe it will also feel familiar to customers overseas.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.885
Wow. It's really pretty.

00:11:25.952 --> 00:11:28.221
Thank you! [employees clap and cheer]

00:11:28.288 --> 00:11:29.375
(Yeongwoo) You're so cool!

00:11:29.442 --> 00:11:31.024
[Jinsang claps loudly]

00:11:31.625 --> 00:11:33.020
I'd like the marketing team

00:11:33.087 --> 00:11:35.462
And the MD team to collaborate on this project.

00:11:35.529 --> 00:11:36.629
(Miyeong, Yeongwoo) Yes, sir!

00:11:39.733 --> 00:11:41.001
[music stops]

00:11:41.068 --> 00:11:42.936
[emotional music plays] [Lee Chan blows]

00:11:44.599 --> 00:11:46.043
[squeaking sound]

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:53.626
(stylist 1) What's that? It's so cute.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:58.384
(Lee Chan) My fan drew this character, and it was so cute I memorized it.

00:11:58.912 --> 00:12:00.708
(stylist 2) But what is this, though?

00:12:00.775 --> 00:12:02.322
Is it a bear or a pig? [stylist 2 laughs]

00:12:03.557 --> 00:12:05.625
(Lee Chan) You're right.

00:12:05.692 --> 00:12:07.694
The nose is a pig's,

00:12:07.761 --> 00:12:09.596
But the ears look like a bear's...

00:12:09.663 --> 00:12:11.577
(stylist 2) It looks more like a pig, right? [stylists laugh]

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:14.600
- (Wonbin) They're asking for you. - (stylist 2) Oh, gosh.

00:12:14.667 --> 00:12:16.236
- (stylist 1) We'll get going now. - (Wonbin) Okay.

00:12:16.303 --> 00:12:17.508
- (stylist 2) Hang in there. - (Wonbin) You too.

00:12:19.352 --> 00:12:21.007
- Here. - (Lee Chan) Thank you.

00:12:22.342 --> 00:12:24.944
What would you have done without that photobook?

00:12:25.772 --> 00:12:28.501
What do you like about it so much? You carry it around like a lucky charm.

00:12:29.224 --> 00:12:30.767
It just...

00:12:33.679 --> 00:12:34.781
Makes me feel better.

00:12:37.082 --> 00:12:37.990
[calm music]

00:12:38.057 --> 00:12:40.526
Whenever I wonder if it's okay to continue my career

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:43.630
Or if I'll be able to keep receiving love from my fans

00:12:44.331 --> 00:12:45.827
And lose confidence,

00:12:47.992 --> 00:12:50.701
(Lee Chan) it feels like this book is telling me to go on.

00:12:51.323 --> 00:12:53.806
(Wonbin) The fan who made you this probably won't even imagine

00:12:53.873 --> 00:12:55.701
[Lee Chan laughs] that it's become your favorite item.

00:12:57.344 --> 00:12:58.834
They're probably not my fan anymore.

00:12:59.659 --> 00:13:00.780
It was ten years ago.

00:13:01.323 --> 00:13:02.773
[Lee Chan, Wonbin laugh]

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:04.117
(Wonbin) Right. It's been ages.

00:13:04.547 --> 00:13:07.853
Who could be that dedicated? [Wonbin sighs]

00:13:08.285 --> 00:13:11.267
(Dareum) I've liked you for 12 years. How would I not know that?

00:13:11.334 --> 00:13:13.993
I know you're a good person.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:17.430
And if you've made an effort to seem like a good person until now,

00:13:17.931 --> 00:13:19.727
That already makes you

00:13:19.794 --> 00:13:21.000
A good enough person.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:24.570
[laughs]

00:13:26.787 --> 00:13:27.900
There is...

00:13:28.522 --> 00:13:29.736
One person. [music fades]

00:13:31.313 --> 00:13:32.981
[ominous music]

00:13:33.881 --> 00:13:35.247
(SE Trading) [birds singing]

00:13:38.886 --> 00:13:41.033
(Miyeong) Why is there a SE Trading car...

00:13:43.856 --> 00:13:44.889
No way...

00:13:44.956 --> 00:13:46.767
Just a moment.

00:13:50.256 --> 00:13:52.665
- (manager) Thank you for accepting. - (shop owner) No problem.

00:13:52.732 --> 00:13:53.835
[shop owner laughs]

00:13:53.902 --> 00:13:55.435
(Mina) Sir.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:57.203
[shop owner reacts]

00:13:57.270 --> 00:14:00.009
(shop owner) Hi, Mina.

00:14:00.076 --> 00:14:02.534
(Mina) What is all this?

00:14:03.393 --> 00:14:05.904
Don't you remember that you were going to sign a contract with us today?

00:14:05.971 --> 00:14:07.946
Well...

00:14:08.013 --> 00:14:10.816
(shop owner) Gosh... I'm sorry.

00:14:10.883 --> 00:14:12.240
SE Trading

00:14:12.307 --> 00:14:15.646
Came to me with a similar proposal,

00:14:15.713 --> 00:14:18.200
And their terms were much better.

00:14:18.267 --> 00:14:20.159
(Mina) But sir...

00:14:20.727 --> 00:14:22.730
I showed this mosaic wrapping cloth

00:14:22.797 --> 00:14:25.300
To you first.

00:14:25.367 --> 00:14:26.967
But how could SE Trading...

00:14:27.034 --> 00:14:27.901
(shop owner) Well...

00:14:27.968 --> 00:14:29.335
I mean, it's possible for you

00:14:30.036 --> 00:14:32.972
To come up with similar ideas, right? [Miyeong scoffs]

00:14:33.039 --> 00:14:33.966
(Mina) What?

00:14:34.033 --> 00:14:35.200
[Miyeong sighs]

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:38.644
(manager) Ms. Nam Dareum. [whoosh sound]

00:14:38.711 --> 00:14:40.714
That's not something you need to worry about, Ms. Nam.

00:14:40.781 --> 00:14:42.582
The event team will handle it. [whoosh sound]

00:14:50.634 --> 00:14:52.234
[somber music]

00:14:54.431 --> 00:14:55.862
(Mina) I'm sorry.

00:14:55.929 --> 00:14:56.996
[Sungwook sighs]

00:14:57.729 --> 00:15:00.133
(Sungwook) How could he cancel on the day of the contract?

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:02.020
They even signed with the same workshop.

00:15:02.087 --> 00:15:04.971
(Miyeong) It seems like they're trying to stop us from bidding on the project.

00:15:05.038 --> 00:15:07.869
(Jinsang) This isn't the first time SE Trading has stabbed us in the back.

00:15:07.936 --> 00:15:09.991
It's pretty clear that they have someone on the inside!

00:15:10.058 --> 00:15:11.777
We have to find out who it is, sir!

00:15:11.844 --> 00:15:14.213
(Sungwook) Are you saying there's a spy among us or what?

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:15.616
(Jinsang) How else would you explain this?

00:15:15.683 --> 00:15:16.756
(Hagi) All right, everyone.

00:15:17.594 --> 00:15:18.642
I also

00:15:20.087 --> 00:15:21.792
Had the same thought once. [music stops]

00:15:23.021 --> 00:15:24.167
But my conclusion

00:15:25.092 --> 00:15:27.760
Was that I shouldn't be so quick to suspect APPELLO employees.

00:15:32.633 --> 00:15:35.928
What's more important now is figuring out another way to win the project.

00:15:35.995 --> 00:15:38.816
Start thinking of alternative items.

00:15:38.883 --> 00:15:39.940
- (Miyeong) Yes, sir. - (Jinsang) Gosh.

00:15:40.007 --> 00:15:42.708
There are only ten days left. How about my dalgona keychain?

00:15:42.775 --> 00:15:43.901
Let's wrap up here.

00:15:43.968 --> 00:15:46.514
(Jinsang) Mr. Kang, my keychain... [door opens]

00:15:46.581 --> 00:15:48.163
- There isn't much time... - I'm sorry, everyone.

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:49.515
(Mina) I'm sorry.

00:15:49.582 --> 00:15:51.463
[Mina inhales] [door opens]

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:03.115
[grunts]

00:16:03.931 --> 00:16:05.195
[phone vibrates]

00:16:07.554 --> 00:16:09.047
[Lee Chan grunts]

00:16:13.079 --> 00:16:14.543
(Lee Chan December schedule) [message notification sound] [sighs]

00:16:15.735 --> 00:16:16.909
[beep sound]

00:16:17.411 --> 00:16:18.466
[sighs]

00:16:28.688 --> 00:16:30.623
(Lee Chan) My "before" photo.

00:16:31.522 --> 00:16:32.925
Still, I'll do my best today.

00:16:34.542 --> 00:16:35.862
Is she busy?

00:16:36.763 --> 00:16:37.734
(Dareum)

00:16:37.759 --> 00:16:39.165
[soft music]

00:16:42.228 --> 00:16:43.703
[laughs] [taps]

00:16:45.223 --> 00:16:46.439
She really does smile a lot.

00:16:50.934 --> 00:16:53.613
[deep sigh]

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.034
[insects chirping] [music fades]

00:17:00.033 --> 00:17:02.721
(Sungwook) Mr. Kang, please just go home today.

00:17:02.788 --> 00:17:04.214
You pulled an all-nighter yesterday too.

00:17:04.281 --> 00:17:05.618
(Hagi) We need to find an alternative.

00:17:05.685 --> 00:17:08.267
If SE Trading wins the K-Wave project just as they launch their platform,

00:17:08.754 --> 00:17:09.855
We'll lose all our investors.

00:17:09.922 --> 00:17:11.497
(Jinsang) Then Mr. Kang, why don't we use my idea...

00:17:11.564 --> 00:17:13.927
(Sungwook) Come on. Can't you read the room?

00:17:13.994 --> 00:17:16.328
You're such a nuisance.

00:17:16.395 --> 00:17:18.438
(Miyeong) Mr. Park, what about the traditional container?

00:17:18.505 --> 00:17:21.407
(Yeongwoo) They said they don't produce wooden containers since the lacquer

00:17:21.474 --> 00:17:22.844
- doesn't dry well in winter. - (Dareum) Okay.

00:17:22.911 --> 00:17:24.720
(Yeongwoo) And mother-of-pearl containers are too expensive.

00:17:24.787 --> 00:17:26.045
(Miyeong) What about traditional hairpins?

00:17:26.112 --> 00:17:27.798
They're already collaborating with a different company.

00:17:27.865 --> 00:17:29.035
[Yeongwoo sighs]

00:17:29.772 --> 00:17:31.901
- (Miyeong) What about traditional paper? - Well,

00:17:31.968 --> 00:17:33.233
They refused the collaboration offer. [Miyeong sighs]

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:35.955
(Hyesu) So we can't work with any of these companies?

00:17:36.022 --> 00:17:37.044
(Yeongwoo) What should we do? [Dareum sighs]

00:17:37.111 --> 00:17:38.720
It's going to be difficult to meet the deadline.

00:17:38.787 --> 00:17:40.294
[Miyeong sighs] Everyone,

00:17:40.361 --> 00:17:42.725
We should still try whatever we can.

00:17:42.792 --> 00:17:44.475
- (Yeongwoo) Yes, ma'am. - (Wontae) Okay. [door opens]

00:17:44.542 --> 00:17:45.898
(Hagi) Ms. Nam.

00:17:45.965 --> 00:17:47.033
Where did you get this?

00:17:47.624 --> 00:17:48.601
(Dareum) What?

00:17:48.979 --> 00:17:50.161
This keychain.

00:17:50.228 --> 00:17:52.074
[intriguing music] [tapping keyboard]

00:17:54.601 --> 00:17:55.667
[mouse clicking] (Dareum) My mom says

00:17:55.734 --> 00:17:57.476
She knows this knot artisan's apprentice

00:17:57.543 --> 00:17:59.312
And received it from them.

00:18:00.218 --> 00:18:01.548
(Korean knot artisan) [mouse clicking]

00:18:01.615 --> 00:18:05.317
(Miyeong) The colors and design are incredible.

00:18:05.384 --> 00:18:06.753
[employees react]

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:08.167
(Hagi) How do we contact her?

00:18:08.701 --> 00:18:09.933
(Dareum) Well... [sighs]

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:12.193
Apparently, she likes to keep to herself,

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:15.127
So there's no guarantee we'll be able to see her.

00:18:15.194 --> 00:18:18.064
But my mom said she'd try talking to her apprentice.

00:18:18.131 --> 00:18:19.567
(Miyeong) Oh, dear. [employees react]

00:18:19.634 --> 00:18:21.133
[music fades]

00:18:22.419 --> 00:18:23.467
[Hagi sighs]

00:18:24.075 --> 00:18:25.655
[intriguing music]

00:18:36.451 --> 00:18:39.333
[message notification sound] (Hagi) I'll pick you up tomorrow morning, so get ready for a business trip.

00:18:39.357 --> 00:18:42.257
Keep this confidential and don't tell anyone where we're going.

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:44.200
[inhales] "Confidential"?

00:18:44.267 --> 00:18:46.324
(Keep this confidential) [whoosh sound]

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:48.795
Then...

00:18:48.862 --> 00:18:52.099
Am I going there alone with Mr. Kang?

00:18:52.166 --> 00:18:53.299
[car approaching]

00:18:54.468 --> 00:18:55.400
Ms. Nam, get in.

00:18:55.467 --> 00:18:56.636
Okay.

00:18:59.492 --> 00:19:00.473
[door closes]

00:19:02.105 --> 00:19:03.275
[music stops]

00:19:04.478 --> 00:19:05.578
[Dareum inhales]

00:19:06.402 --> 00:19:07.634
But...

00:19:07.701 --> 00:19:11.040
Why are we keeping this business trip a secret?

00:19:11.107 --> 00:19:12.752
We can't guarantee that SE Trading

00:19:13.287 --> 00:19:15.121
Won't stab us in the back twice.

00:19:15.822 --> 00:19:18.058
(Hagi) I want to proceed with this quietly until the contract

00:19:18.125 --> 00:19:19.325
Is finalized.

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:20.860
[Dareum reacts]

00:19:21.534 --> 00:19:22.261
(Dareum) Right.

00:19:22.328 --> 00:19:24.888
We don't even know where the artisan is,

00:19:24.955 --> 00:19:26.808
So it'll be difficult for them to steal this item.

00:19:26.875 --> 00:19:30.036
But is there a reason why you're taking me?

00:19:32.918 --> 00:19:35.240
Well, you have the closest connection with the artisan.

00:19:35.307 --> 00:19:36.245
(Dareum) Oh...

00:19:37.010 --> 00:19:37.943
(Hagi) And more than anything,

00:19:38.434 --> 00:19:39.979
You're the only one I can trust completely

00:19:41.217 --> 00:19:42.615
At the moment.

00:19:45.819 --> 00:19:47.367
[bright music]

00:19:49.501 --> 00:19:50.501
[scoffs]

00:19:51.024 --> 00:19:53.693
Did you forget how you used to think I was a spy?

00:19:54.193 --> 00:19:55.227
[Dareum laughs]

00:19:55.294 --> 00:19:57.630
Just leave this to me.

00:19:57.697 --> 00:20:01.701
I, Nam Dareum, will show you around Jungsan.

00:20:02.868 --> 00:20:04.236
[laughs]

00:20:09.116 --> 00:20:10.348
[Dareum laughs]

00:20:11.122 --> 00:20:13.464
(Miyeong) Okay. Please take care of that. [music stops]

00:20:13.531 --> 00:20:14.801
All right. Thank you.

00:20:15.512 --> 00:20:16.515
[Miyeong sighs]

00:20:17.008 --> 00:20:19.700
I just contacted the supplier for natural silk thread.

00:20:19.767 --> 00:20:21.718
We'll be able to get a sample by tomorrow,

00:20:21.785 --> 00:20:25.231
So I want you to come up with ideas for what kind of products we can make.

00:20:25.298 --> 00:20:26.113
- (Yeongwoo) Yes, ma'am! - (Wontae) Okay.

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:27.059
(Miyeong) Okay.

00:20:28.103 --> 00:20:28.977
[clears throat]

00:20:29.044 --> 00:20:30.567
But where did Ms. Nam

00:20:30.634 --> 00:20:34.060
(Hyesu) go to speak with the knot artisan?

00:20:34.127 --> 00:20:37.036
Did Mr. Kang go with her? [ominous music]

00:20:38.372 --> 00:20:39.267
I'm not sure.

00:20:39.334 --> 00:20:41.667
I don't know the exact details either. [laughs]

00:20:42.385 --> 00:20:43.676
Okay.

00:20:52.218 --> 00:20:54.050
[street sounds] [lively music]

00:21:03.887 --> 00:21:05.564
[car beeps] [birds singing] (Dareum) Wow...

00:21:05.934 --> 00:21:08.033
I can't believe we're passing by this place.

00:21:09.494 --> 00:21:11.501
That's the neighborhood where I used to live.

00:21:12.059 --> 00:21:14.362
And there's a market this way.

00:21:14.429 --> 00:21:15.700
[Dareum inhales]

00:21:15.767 --> 00:21:18.110
And there's even a lake park over there.

00:21:20.212 --> 00:21:22.815
(Hagi) You really do know this place inside out.

00:21:22.882 --> 00:21:24.851
Of course.

00:21:24.918 --> 00:21:27.887
Everyone in this neighborhood knows me.

00:21:31.367 --> 00:21:32.424
[music stops]

00:21:39.933 --> 00:21:41.300
Is that "Nam Dareum"

00:21:42.934 --> 00:21:44.734
This Nam Dareum right here?

00:21:45.799 --> 00:21:47.167
[playful music]

00:21:47.191 --> 00:21:49.409
(Kim Mija's daughter Nam Dareum accepted by SE Trading) [whoosh sound]

00:21:49.476 --> 00:21:50.509
[gasps]

00:21:51.345 --> 00:21:52.444
What is that?

00:21:53.247 --> 00:21:54.234
I guess...

00:21:54.847 --> 00:21:56.531
You really are a local celebrity. [Dareum sighs]

00:21:56.598 --> 00:21:59.412
(Dareum) I can't believe this.

00:22:01.655 --> 00:22:02.956
[taps]

00:22:03.524 --> 00:22:04.834
[call connecting sound] [Dareum sighs]

00:22:05.292 --> 00:22:06.392
Mom...

00:22:07.094 --> 00:22:08.227
Mom.

00:22:08.801 --> 00:22:11.233
What is this banner? Take that down.

00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:12.299
Don't be silly.

00:22:12.366 --> 00:22:14.696
I paid for that. Why would I take it down?

00:22:14.763 --> 00:22:17.561
I'm hanging that there for at least six months. [Mija laughs]

00:22:17.628 --> 00:22:19.532
[Dareum sighs] (Mija) I guess you're here, then.

00:22:19.599 --> 00:22:20.874
Aren't you coming to see me?

00:22:20.941 --> 00:22:22.775
I'm here for work, so I can't.

00:22:23.509 --> 00:22:25.267
What about what I asked for? [music stops]

00:22:25.965 --> 00:22:29.114
Well... Try going to your old high school.

00:22:29.181 --> 00:22:31.085
(Mija) She'll only have a brief moment after lunchtime.

00:22:31.152 --> 00:22:32.818
Okay.

00:22:33.453 --> 00:22:36.388
Thank you so much, Mom. I'll call you again later.

00:22:37.124 --> 00:22:38.090
(Dareum) Bye.

00:22:38.932 --> 00:22:40.033
[call ending sound] [camera snaps]

00:22:40.100 --> 00:22:41.579
[intriguing music]

00:22:41.646 --> 00:22:44.463
Stop. Why are you taking photos of that?

00:22:45.918 --> 00:22:47.734
You were the pride of the whole neighborhood.

00:22:48.535 --> 00:22:50.135
(Hagi) "SE Trading,

00:22:50.934 --> 00:22:52.338
Ms. Nam Dareum."

00:22:57.233 --> 00:22:58.277
[groans]

00:22:59.300 --> 00:23:01.047
[upbeat music]

00:23:14.214 --> 00:23:16.742
(Hagi) The whole neighborhood must bring back memories for you.

00:23:17.173 --> 00:23:18.398
(Dareum) Yes.

00:23:18.465 --> 00:23:19.364
[Dareum laughs]

00:23:19.431 --> 00:23:22.534
But it feels strange to be here with you, Mr. Kang.

00:23:24.022 --> 00:23:25.037
[gasps]

00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:27.773
(Dareum) My favorite snack bar!

00:23:30.341 --> 00:23:31.677
[car engine revs]

00:23:32.534 --> 00:23:34.580
I used to go there every day. [music stops]

00:23:35.516 --> 00:23:36.582
[Dareum grunts]

00:23:43.891 --> 00:23:45.067
Walk on the inside.

00:23:45.602 --> 00:23:46.759
Okay.

00:23:51.145 --> 00:23:55.334
[inhales] He does seem oddly sweet.

00:23:59.883 --> 00:24:01.908
(guard) If you wait over there for a moment,

00:24:01.975 --> 00:24:03.933
I'll call the cafeteria.

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:05.801
(Dareum) Okay. Thank you.

00:24:06.322 --> 00:24:07.279
(Hagi) Thank you.

00:24:08.149 --> 00:24:09.366
Over here.

00:24:09.433 --> 00:24:10.416
(Hagi) Right.

00:24:11.236 --> 00:24:12.718
[wistful music]

00:24:18.067 --> 00:24:19.933
[students chatter]

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:22.067
(Dareum) Wow, it's been a long time.

00:24:23.634 --> 00:24:25.757
- Why don't we sit down for a bit? - (Hagi) Sure.

00:24:26.272 --> 00:24:27.300
[Dareum exclaims]

00:24:29.069 --> 00:24:30.701
(Hagi) So this is your old school?

00:24:31.224 --> 00:24:32.204
(Dareum) Yes.

00:24:34.764 --> 00:24:35.908
[sighs]

00:24:47.100 --> 00:24:48.454
[whoosh sound]

00:25:01.301 --> 00:25:02.634
I used to sit here

00:25:03.959 --> 00:25:05.637
And listen to music often. [music fades]

00:25:07.302 --> 00:25:08.474
Everything's still the same.

00:25:10.601 --> 00:25:12.700
- (student 1) Wow, he's so handsome. - (Dareum) What? [students squeal]

00:25:12.767 --> 00:25:14.050
What?

00:25:14.117 --> 00:25:16.057
[whoosh sound] [exciting music] (student 1) Hi. Are you a celebrity?

00:25:16.124 --> 00:25:17.884
- (Hagi) No, I'm not. - (student 2) Are you an actor? A model?

00:25:17.951 --> 00:25:20.271
(student 3) You're so handsome. Do you have social media?

00:25:20.338 --> 00:25:21.585
(student 4) Can I take a selfie with you?

00:25:21.652 --> 00:25:23.783
[Hagi grunts] (student 3) You're so handsome.

00:25:23.850 --> 00:25:26.200
(Dareum) Oh, gosh... [camera snaps] [students chatter]

00:25:26.267 --> 00:25:28.483
- (Dareum) You guys... - (Hagi) I'm not a celebrity.

00:25:28.550 --> 00:25:30.034
(student 1) You're so handsome!

00:25:30.101 --> 00:25:31.430
[students continue chattering]

00:25:32.099 --> 00:25:33.337
[Dareum grunts]

00:25:33.404 --> 00:25:34.567
[snatches] [Dareum grunts]

00:25:34.634 --> 00:25:35.869
(student 2) What?

00:25:35.936 --> 00:25:37.582
(students) Wait! [upbeat music]

00:25:54.657 --> 00:25:56.133
[students chatter]

00:26:01.004 --> 00:26:02.667
[music stops] (Byeola) What?

00:26:02.734 --> 00:26:04.033
Isn't that Dareum?

00:26:04.606 --> 00:26:06.266
(Insadong, my house) All right, everyone. [bright music]

00:26:06.333 --> 00:26:10.302
(Today's Mission: Find a Hot-Selling Item) Today, I'll show you how I prepare for a buying trip.

00:26:10.369 --> 00:26:11.668
All right. [sparkling sound]

00:26:11.692 --> 00:26:12.610
(Aseul Aseul Enter website)

00:26:12.634 --> 00:26:14.440
I don't have a car,

00:26:15.034 --> 00:26:17.142
(Licensed for years, taking a cab again) so I usually take a cab to the market.

00:26:17.209 --> 00:26:18.534
[sparkling sound]

00:26:19.213 --> 00:26:21.537
This is where I bought the strawberry panties.

00:26:21.604 --> 00:26:22.595
I'm with the owner here.

00:26:22.662 --> 00:26:24.816
I'm going to try selling this sexy underwear.

00:26:24.883 --> 00:26:28.153
I like to see and feel the products in person before I buy them.

00:26:28.220 --> 00:26:29.890
(Mimi) You still have those sitting in inventory.

00:26:29.957 --> 00:26:31.556
[falling sound]

00:26:31.623 --> 00:26:32.825
[bright music plays]

00:26:33.293 --> 00:26:34.667
[tapping keyboard] [music stops]

00:26:35.629 --> 00:26:37.396
(Seula) I told you to be quiet while I recorded.

00:26:37.817 --> 00:26:38.961
[Mimi sighs]

00:26:40.294 --> 00:26:42.356
What are you doing instead of working these days?

00:26:44.226 --> 00:26:45.433
This is work.

00:26:45.500 --> 00:26:46.305
[scoffs]

00:26:46.673 --> 00:26:49.638
(Seula) These days, you have to promote your products through videos.

00:26:50.210 --> 00:26:52.810
Just wait and see. Orders are going to start pouring in soon.

00:26:52.877 --> 00:26:54.213
(Mimi) Yeah, right.

00:26:54.280 --> 00:26:56.949
Refund requests poured in after you sold those padded bras last time.

00:26:58.238 --> 00:26:59.785
(Seula) Hey. [cat hissing sound]

00:26:59.852 --> 00:27:01.386
I got scammed because I was new to the business. [intriguing music]

00:27:01.453 --> 00:27:02.554
How was I supposed to know [whoosh sound]

00:27:02.621 --> 00:27:04.534
That the pads would move to the side? [swishing sound]

00:27:05.659 --> 00:27:06.635
That's what I mean.

00:27:06.702 --> 00:27:07.993
(Mimi) You should stick to what you know.

00:27:08.060 --> 00:27:10.429
Why sell sexy underwear that you've never even worn before? [cat meowing sound]

00:27:10.496 --> 00:27:11.698
You idiot.

00:27:11.765 --> 00:27:13.067
Jeez...

00:27:14.399 --> 00:27:15.858
[phone vibrating]

00:27:15.925 --> 00:27:16.902
[Seula exclaims]

00:27:17.538 --> 00:27:19.204
I must've received an order.

00:27:24.351 --> 00:27:25.744
[message notification sound] What?

00:27:26.613 --> 00:27:28.217
Dareum must be visiting our hometown.

00:27:28.284 --> 00:27:29.308
(Mimi) What?

00:27:30.250 --> 00:27:31.434
- Without even telling us? - (Seula) Right?

00:27:31.501 --> 00:27:35.001
[message notification sound] (Byeola) Seula, Dareum came to our school with this handsome guy!

00:27:35.068 --> 00:27:36.454
[message notification sound] It must be her boyfriend!

00:27:36.516 --> 00:27:37.634
[message notification sound]

00:27:39.026 --> 00:27:40.966
(Seula) What? Boyfriend?

00:27:41.033 --> 00:27:42.311
(Mimi) Wow...

00:27:43.292 --> 00:27:45.868
Who was that guy again?

00:27:46.527 --> 00:27:47.599
[music stops]

00:27:47.666 --> 00:27:48.600
[Hagi sighs] [Dareum grunts]

00:27:48.667 --> 00:27:49.736
[Hagi clears throat]

00:27:49.803 --> 00:27:50.897
[Dareum laughs]

00:27:52.259 --> 00:27:55.467
You're really popular with the high school girls.

00:27:55.933 --> 00:27:56.942
[Dareum laughs]

00:27:57.009 --> 00:27:58.777
You were popular back in school, weren't you?

00:28:00.767 --> 00:28:01.713
(Hagi) Well...

00:28:02.216 --> 00:28:03.549
A bit, I guess.

00:28:04.985 --> 00:28:06.251
[laughs awkwardly]

00:28:06.720 --> 00:28:07.619
Right.

00:28:08.178 --> 00:28:09.354
You really...

00:28:09.923 --> 00:28:11.601
Don't lie. [laughs awkwardly]

00:28:12.392 --> 00:28:13.392
(Hagi) What about you?

00:28:14.728 --> 00:28:16.795
What were you like in school?

00:28:18.398 --> 00:28:19.398
[Dareum laughs]

00:28:19.766 --> 00:28:20.999
(Dareum) What do you think?

00:28:22.668 --> 00:28:24.567
Cheerful, like you are now.

00:28:24.634 --> 00:28:25.405
[Dareum reacts]

00:28:25.472 --> 00:28:26.872
Full of energy... [Dareum reacts]

00:28:28.309 --> 00:28:29.767
(Hagi) And a social butterfly

00:28:30.427 --> 00:28:31.678
Who knew everyone?

00:28:31.745 --> 00:28:33.508
[Dareum reacts]

00:28:33.575 --> 00:28:35.180
Wrong! [Dareum laughs]

00:28:36.083 --> 00:28:37.167
To be honest,

00:28:39.651 --> 00:28:40.986
I didn't have any friends for a while.

00:28:42.596 --> 00:28:44.121
[lonely music]

00:28:45.228 --> 00:28:46.558
Even during lunchtime,

00:28:47.567 --> 00:28:49.789
I sat alone for most of the time.

00:28:50.731 --> 00:28:51.634
So

00:28:52.506 --> 00:28:54.066
Seeing kids like that

00:28:56.205 --> 00:28:57.369
Bothers me a little.

00:29:05.041 --> 00:29:07.179
It's a feeling only people who've been alone can understand.

00:29:08.815 --> 00:29:09.982
(Hagi) Maybe that's why

00:29:11.104 --> 00:29:13.719
You're always considerate of other people's

00:29:15.960 --> 00:29:16.888
Feelings.

00:29:19.159 --> 00:29:20.125
[laughs]

00:29:22.291 --> 00:29:23.295
(Dareum) Still,

00:29:23.885 --> 00:29:26.400
I have a lot more good memories here.

00:29:26.467 --> 00:29:28.439
I found someone who gave me strength,

00:29:28.870 --> 00:29:29.801
So I was able to fight through it.

00:29:31.138 --> 00:29:32.162
Who's that?

00:29:32.229 --> 00:29:33.478
[Dareum inhales]

00:29:33.545 --> 00:29:35.033
(Dareum) Well...

00:29:35.642 --> 00:29:36.804
My...

00:29:36.871 --> 00:29:38.234
[laughs]

00:29:38.946 --> 00:29:39.968
First love.

00:29:41.181 --> 00:29:42.347
[Dareum laughs]

00:29:43.517 --> 00:29:45.546
Seeing him work hard

00:29:45.613 --> 00:29:49.067
Motivated me to work harder as well.

00:29:49.746 --> 00:29:50.856
Anyway,

00:29:51.667 --> 00:29:53.025
I'm very grateful for him.

00:29:57.296 --> 00:29:58.263
I'm glad...

00:30:00.521 --> 00:30:01.867
(Hagi) you had someone like that

00:30:03.022 --> 00:30:04.236
Back then.

00:30:10.804 --> 00:30:11.910
[laughs]

00:30:15.593 --> 00:30:16.983
(Eunjeong) Excuse me...

00:30:17.050 --> 00:30:18.417
[music fades]

00:30:19.953 --> 00:30:22.263
Are you the people looking for my mentor?

00:30:22.330 --> 00:30:23.455
(Dareum) Yes!

00:30:24.014 --> 00:30:26.291
- Hello. - (Eunjeong) Hello.

00:30:27.319 --> 00:30:28.431
(Eunjeong) Well...

00:30:29.464 --> 00:30:32.336
I did come because Mija asked me to, but...

00:30:32.403 --> 00:30:33.966
If you just tell us the location,

00:30:34.033 --> 00:30:35.601
We'll try talking to her ourselves.

00:30:36.819 --> 00:30:39.083
Please don't tell her you got the address from me.

00:30:39.150 --> 00:30:40.540
(Dareum) Of course.

00:30:40.607 --> 00:30:42.000
It won't be easy...

00:30:42.636 --> 00:30:43.980
(Eunjeong) But do your best.

00:30:44.047 --> 00:30:45.154
Good luck!

00:30:45.221 --> 00:30:46.354
[ding sound] (Dareum) What?

00:30:46.720 --> 00:30:48.046
[intriguing music]

00:30:50.563 --> 00:30:51.449
[music stops]

00:30:51.516 --> 00:30:53.200
[birds singing] [lively music]

00:30:55.889 --> 00:30:58.176
(Dareum) Excuse me. Anyone here?

00:31:04.863 --> 00:31:05.697
Hello.

00:31:06.039 --> 00:31:06.998
Hello.

00:31:23.734 --> 00:31:25.250
(Hagi) Hello. [man 1 reacts]

00:31:25.317 --> 00:31:27.233
Do you know where Ms. Im is?

00:31:27.300 --> 00:31:28.920
(man 1) She's over there.

00:31:28.987 --> 00:31:30.400
- (Hagi) Thank you. - (Dareum) Thank you.

00:31:30.467 --> 00:31:31.757
[music fades]

00:31:35.534 --> 00:31:39.133
(woman 1) Wow, look at the color. It looks delicious.

00:31:39.200 --> 00:31:39.998
[woman 1 exclaims]

00:31:40.065 --> 00:31:41.538
- Bring some more chives. - (woman 2) Okay.

00:31:41.605 --> 00:31:42.569
- (woman 1) Good. - (Hagi) Hello.

00:31:42.636 --> 00:31:43.728
(Dareum) Hello.

00:31:44.638 --> 00:31:45.501
(woman 1) What?

00:31:45.868 --> 00:31:46.816
Who are you?

00:31:46.883 --> 00:31:50.213
(Hagi) We're from a company in Seoul called APPELLO.

00:31:50.280 --> 00:31:52.024
This is Ms. Im Cheongrim's home, right?

00:31:52.091 --> 00:31:52.967
(woman 1) What?

00:31:53.034 --> 00:31:54.898
How did you know she was here?

00:31:54.965 --> 00:31:56.093
[Hagi exhales]

00:31:57.115 --> 00:31:58.106
Cheongrim!

00:31:58.173 --> 00:31:59.820
Someone's here for you!

00:31:59.887 --> 00:32:01.033
Come out here!

00:32:02.287 --> 00:32:03.355
[door opens]

00:32:03.850 --> 00:32:05.515
[dramatic traditional Korean music] [door closes]

00:32:20.774 --> 00:32:22.494
[music stops] [birds singing]

00:32:23.611 --> 00:32:24.876
[elegant traditional Korean music]

00:32:32.000 --> 00:32:34.000
(Certificate of Merit for Craftsmanship Transmission)

00:32:41.278 --> 00:32:42.234
[Dareum grunts]

00:32:42.996 --> 00:32:44.225
[rustles]

00:32:44.891 --> 00:32:46.272
Ma'am,

00:32:46.339 --> 00:32:48.700
This is the proposal we've made in advance.

00:32:48.724 --> 00:32:50.024
(Traditional Knotting Project)

00:32:54.783 --> 00:32:57.292
(Hagi) APPELLO is a fashion platform that curates designer brands

00:32:57.359 --> 00:32:59.579
From Korea and around the world.

00:32:59.646 --> 00:33:01.381
And we're trying to bring traditional craftsmanship

00:33:01.405 --> 00:33:02.647
And contemporary design together.

00:33:03.902 --> 00:33:06.431
We believe we can introduce your work to the world...

00:33:06.498 --> 00:33:07.968
What about production?

00:33:08.035 --> 00:33:09.133
(Hagi) Don't worry, ma'am.

00:33:09.790 --> 00:33:11.790
The factory has more than enough technical expertise

00:33:12.560 --> 00:33:13.425
[thuds]

00:33:14.011 --> 00:33:15.332
(Cheongrim) Factory?

00:33:17.465 --> 00:33:18.634
Forget it.

00:33:20.699 --> 00:33:22.966
(Hagi) If you're not happy with the factory we've chosen...

00:33:23.033 --> 00:33:23.963
(Cheongrim) No.

00:33:24.030 --> 00:33:26.300
I have no intention of working with profiteers.

00:33:27.875 --> 00:33:28.740
[exhales]

00:33:28.807 --> 00:33:29.908
Get out.

00:33:35.757 --> 00:33:37.400
[birds singing] [faint dog barking]

00:33:42.317 --> 00:33:43.412
[Dareum sighs]

00:33:44.399 --> 00:33:46.004
What should we do?

00:33:46.071 --> 00:33:47.049
[faint sigh]

00:33:49.148 --> 00:33:51.363
(Hagi) You've already done more than enough here.

00:33:52.097 --> 00:33:54.640
I'll give you a ride to the terminal, so head back to Seoul first.

00:33:54.707 --> 00:33:56.801
What about you, Mr. Kang?

00:33:58.120 --> 00:33:58.933
[uplifting music]

00:33:59.000 --> 00:34:00.772
I'm going to convince Ms. Im.

00:34:01.642 --> 00:34:03.033
(Hagi) Seeing her work in person

00:34:03.477 --> 00:34:04.509
Made me certain of this.

00:34:07.447 --> 00:34:08.474
[sighs]

00:34:08.916 --> 00:34:09.881
Then...

00:34:11.021 --> 00:34:12.350
I'll stay too.

00:34:13.253 --> 00:34:14.898
I'll do whatever I can to help.

00:34:15.756 --> 00:34:16.801
What are you going to do?

00:34:17.350 --> 00:34:18.456
(Dareum) Well...

00:34:20.337 --> 00:34:22.260
Whatever I can.

00:34:25.332 --> 00:34:26.398
(Hagi) Ms. Nam.

00:34:26.835 --> 00:34:28.341
[door creaks] [music stops]

00:34:29.570 --> 00:34:30.601
[smacking sound]

00:34:31.870 --> 00:34:33.071
[exhales]

00:34:33.138 --> 00:34:34.245
[Dareum grunts] [lively music]

00:34:34.312 --> 00:34:35.539
(Dareum) Gosh! [woman 1 grunts]

00:34:35.606 --> 00:34:37.342
As a fellow Korean,

00:34:37.409 --> 00:34:39.581
I can't just leave when you're making

00:34:39.648 --> 00:34:40.788
A huge pile of kimchi?

00:34:40.855 --> 00:34:42.816
I'll help you out a little.

00:34:42.883 --> 00:34:45.534
Should I put the seasoning inside the cabbages?

00:34:46.109 --> 00:34:47.000
[woman 1 laughs]

00:34:47.067 --> 00:34:50.021
My goodness. You look so frail.

00:34:50.088 --> 00:34:51.600
Have you even made kimchi before?

00:34:51.667 --> 00:34:53.758
- (Dareum) What? - (woman 1) It's no easy task, you know.

00:34:53.825 --> 00:34:55.084
(Dareum) What? [woman 1 laughs]

00:34:55.151 --> 00:34:59.397
I've actually had some experience helping my mom.

00:34:59.464 --> 00:35:01.499
[Dareum, woman 1 laugh]

00:35:03.171 --> 00:35:04.204
Hurry up and help out here.

00:35:04.271 --> 00:35:05.133
Oh, right.

00:35:07.868 --> 00:35:09.447
(woman 1) Spread the seasoning inside.

00:35:09.514 --> 00:35:11.133
- (Dareum) Like this? - (woman 1) Yes, that's it.

00:35:12.112 --> 00:35:13.878
(Hagi) Hi,

00:35:13.945 --> 00:35:15.769
There's an extra set of strong hands from Seoul here.

00:35:15.836 --> 00:35:17.734
[women laugh]

00:35:18.601 --> 00:35:20.428
[women chatter] That must be heavy. Let me help.

00:35:20.923 --> 00:35:22.621
This must be pretty heavy.

00:35:23.090 --> 00:35:24.422
[Hagi grunts] [comical sound]

00:35:25.829 --> 00:35:26.924
[grunts]

00:35:26.991 --> 00:35:28.059
That's a lot.

00:35:28.126 --> 00:35:29.703
(woman 1) He's pretty frail too.

00:35:29.770 --> 00:35:32.197
[woman 1 laughs] - (Dareum) I'm sure he'll be useful. - (Hagi) I'll put this here.

00:35:32.831 --> 00:35:35.914
(woman 1) Both of you are so frail. [Hagi grunts]

00:35:35.981 --> 00:35:37.737
He has no strength at all.

00:35:37.804 --> 00:35:39.804
- I'm sure he'll be of some use. - (man 2) Help me out here.

00:35:39.871 --> 00:35:41.327
(woman 1) He looks like he won't even be able to hold chopsticks.

00:35:41.394 --> 00:35:42.507
[everyone laughs] [music fades]

00:35:42.574 --> 00:35:43.675
(I only see you, Park Seojin) [birds singing]

00:35:46.811 --> 00:35:47.849
(Mija) Hey!

00:35:47.916 --> 00:35:49.514
[music: Park Seojin's "Push Push"] - <i>Scrub, scrub</i> - (Eunjeong) Mija!

00:35:49.581 --> 00:35:51.352
(Mija) <i>With love</i>

00:35:51.419 --> 00:35:54.380
(Eunjeong) <i>Scrub the grime in your heart</i>

00:35:54.447 --> 00:35:57.290
[Mija cheers] [Eunjeong laughs]

00:35:57.357 --> 00:35:59.025
[Eunjeong, Mija cheer]

00:35:59.092 --> 00:36:00.825
Did you talk to Dareum?

00:36:00.892 --> 00:36:01.823
Yes, of course.

00:36:01.890 --> 00:36:03.962
(Eunjeong) She came with a colleague. [music stops]

00:36:04.029 --> 00:36:05.221
She looked really busy.

00:36:05.288 --> 00:36:06.466
- (Mija) Right? - (Eunjeong) Yeah.

00:36:06.533 --> 00:36:09.000
She seems to be having a tough time after entering a big company

00:36:09.067 --> 00:36:10.661
(Mija) in Seoul.

00:36:10.728 --> 00:36:14.701
Well, it's only natural. It's SE Trading.

00:36:15.135 --> 00:36:16.357
She must have loads of work.

00:36:16.424 --> 00:36:17.563
SE Trading?

00:36:17.630 --> 00:36:18.845
SE? That's strange.

00:36:18.912 --> 00:36:20.434
It wasn't SE. [screeching sound]

00:36:21.682 --> 00:36:22.614
What do you mean,

00:36:23.097 --> 00:36:24.282
It wasn't SE?

00:36:24.701 --> 00:36:26.120
- Pello. - (Mija) What?

00:36:26.187 --> 00:36:27.585
(Eunjeong) It was something like...

00:36:28.021 --> 00:36:29.427
Pello or something.

00:36:29.494 --> 00:36:31.043
- (Mija) What? - (Eunjeong) Hang on. [rustles]

00:36:32.025 --> 00:36:33.758
Right. APPELLO.

00:36:33.825 --> 00:36:35.160
It was APPELLO.

00:36:35.227 --> 00:36:36.227
(Mija) What?

00:36:37.128 --> 00:36:38.131
(Nam Dareum)

00:36:38.155 --> 00:36:39.097
What is this?

00:36:40.178 --> 00:36:41.366
"APPELLO"?

00:36:42.169 --> 00:36:43.902
[comical sound] [playful music]

00:36:50.934 --> 00:36:52.110
[plops]

00:36:52.911 --> 00:36:53.904
[woman 2 grunts]

00:36:56.714 --> 00:36:58.285
- (Hagi) Ms. Nam. - (Dareum) Yes?

00:36:58.352 --> 00:36:59.747
(Hagi) Be more thorough.

00:36:59.814 --> 00:37:03.056
Don't just spread it. You have to coat the leaves.

00:37:03.123 --> 00:37:04.767
Work it into the layers like this.

00:37:04.834 --> 00:37:05.957
Let it seep in.

00:37:06.388 --> 00:37:07.392
Like this.

00:37:08.960 --> 00:37:11.729
(Dareum) Like this?

00:37:11.796 --> 00:37:12.873
Like this?

00:37:12.940 --> 00:37:15.001
Look, it's already gone completely limp.

00:37:15.068 --> 00:37:16.679
Do it more gently, okay?

00:37:16.746 --> 00:37:18.098
With sincerity.

00:37:18.165 --> 00:37:19.473
[laughs awkwardly]

00:37:19.540 --> 00:37:21.544
You seem very thorough...

00:37:22.042 --> 00:37:23.516
With everything.

00:37:23.583 --> 00:37:24.842
When I start something,

00:37:24.909 --> 00:37:27.378
I have to see it through until the end.

00:37:28.182 --> 00:37:29.577
[laughs awkwardly]

00:37:32.386 --> 00:37:33.485
[music stops]

00:37:34.942 --> 00:37:35.987
[Hagi sighs]

00:37:36.721 --> 00:37:37.998
I'm wearing these gloves again.

00:37:38.065 --> 00:37:38.990
(Dareum) What?

00:37:39.819 --> 00:37:40.760
[sighs]

00:37:40.827 --> 00:37:43.161
I thought I'd never wear them again after taking my cast off. [squishing]

00:37:46.077 --> 00:37:48.401
(Dareum) Mr. Kang.

00:37:48.468 --> 00:37:50.501
Did you actually wear...

00:37:51.588 --> 00:37:52.637
Those rubber gloves?

00:37:53.040 --> 00:37:54.786
[bubble popping sounds] [intriguing music]

00:37:56.342 --> 00:37:57.389
[bubble popping sound]

00:37:57.456 --> 00:37:59.365
[laughs]

00:38:00.532 --> 00:38:01.739
(Dareum) Back then, you said,

00:38:01.806 --> 00:38:04.582
[comical sound] "I have to watch my front and back when I'm with you"

00:38:04.649 --> 00:38:07.000
[bubble popping sound] and snapped at me.

00:38:08.722 --> 00:38:09.834
But I guess you wore them.

00:38:12.223 --> 00:38:14.292
Fine, I did!

00:38:14.359 --> 00:38:15.862
[Dareum laughs] (Hagi) Happy?

00:38:15.929 --> 00:38:18.062
(Dareum) You said you wouldn't wear them.

00:38:18.129 --> 00:38:19.664
Jeez...

00:38:21.391 --> 00:38:22.516
(Dareum) They were nice, right?

00:38:22.583 --> 00:38:23.939
[Dareum laughs]

00:38:24.006 --> 00:38:25.195
(Hagi) Whatever.

00:38:25.262 --> 00:38:26.293
Just do this properly.

00:38:26.360 --> 00:38:27.964
(Dareum) I am.

00:38:28.031 --> 00:38:29.743
(Hagi) They're all limp... [doors open] [music stops]

00:38:29.810 --> 00:38:31.776
(Eunjeong) Mija!

00:38:35.587 --> 00:38:36.581
Mom.

00:38:39.417 --> 00:38:41.779
[Dareum grunts] [Mija sighs]

00:38:43.555 --> 00:38:44.661
How did you...

00:38:44.728 --> 00:38:46.291
[huffs]

00:38:46.920 --> 00:38:48.267
[sighs]

00:38:49.296 --> 00:38:50.363
[thuds]

00:38:50.430 --> 00:38:52.247
(Mija) You! [Mija huffs]

00:38:52.900 --> 00:38:54.200
Give me those gloves!

00:38:55.201 --> 00:38:57.640
- (Dareum) What? - Just go

00:38:57.707 --> 00:38:59.653
And help them move the containers.

00:38:59.720 --> 00:39:01.439
Give me the gloves!

00:39:02.666 --> 00:39:03.829
(Dareum) Okay...

00:39:03.896 --> 00:39:04.968
[huffs]

00:39:07.541 --> 00:39:08.834
[calm music]

00:39:12.428 --> 00:39:13.518
(Mija) Move.

00:39:16.983 --> 00:39:18.567
[squelches] [sniffles]

00:39:18.634 --> 00:39:19.656
Mom...

00:39:22.696 --> 00:39:23.777
Ms. Im.

00:39:27.614 --> 00:39:28.718
[Mija reacts]

00:39:30.204 --> 00:39:31.469
Ms. Im.

00:39:32.478 --> 00:39:35.367
Can you please help my daughter out?

00:39:36.614 --> 00:39:39.501
She never does anything halfheartedly.

00:39:39.568 --> 00:39:42.767
If you help her, I'm sure she'll do an amazing job.

00:39:43.784 --> 00:39:44.667
Right.

00:39:45.189 --> 00:39:46.204
[Mija laughs awkwardly]

00:39:46.271 --> 00:39:48.321
This looks amazing. [laughs]

00:39:48.388 --> 00:39:50.694
You bought really good cabbages.

00:39:51.434 --> 00:39:52.667
They look great.

00:39:55.701 --> 00:39:59.197
You have to wrap them thoroughly like this.

00:40:00.234 --> 00:40:01.633
And add lots of seasoning.

00:40:03.598 --> 00:40:04.636
[Mija grunts]

00:40:05.670 --> 00:40:06.721
[music stops]

00:40:06.788 --> 00:40:07.868
[Minwoo sighs]

00:40:09.966 --> 00:40:11.009
Look at you.

00:40:11.577 --> 00:40:12.744
You're looking pretty good today.

00:40:13.278 --> 00:40:16.771
Maybe I shouldn't have applied for a group lesson.

00:40:16.838 --> 00:40:18.701
If everyone falls in love with me,

00:40:19.319 --> 00:40:20.780
That would be troublesome.

00:40:20.847 --> 00:40:22.120
[taps] [smacks lips]

00:40:22.923 --> 00:40:25.256
(Mimi) Take a long step back,

00:40:25.323 --> 00:40:26.461
And move down.

00:40:26.528 --> 00:40:28.149
One. [intriguing music] [trembling sound]

00:40:28.595 --> 00:40:29.627
Two.

00:40:30.130 --> 00:40:31.531
[Minwoo exhales] One.

00:40:31.598 --> 00:40:32.698
[Minwoo grunts]

00:40:33.021 --> 00:40:34.834
Two. [Minwoo exhales]

00:40:35.167 --> 00:40:36.334
One.

00:40:36.935 --> 00:40:37.869
Minwoo, lower your arms. [music fades]

00:40:37.936 --> 00:40:39.303
[Minwoo gasps] [swish sound] [playful music]

00:40:39.370 --> 00:40:40.978
(Mimi) Tighten your core. [Minwoo gasps] [creaking sound]

00:40:41.045 --> 00:40:42.986
Straighten your back and tighten your core. [whoosh sound]

00:40:43.053 --> 00:40:46.077
[Minwoo grunts] Straighten your back. Tighten your core.

00:40:46.144 --> 00:40:47.834
Minwoo, lower your arms. [Minwoo groans]

00:40:47.901 --> 00:40:48.946
Tighten your core. [Minwoo gasps]

00:40:49.013 --> 00:40:51.000
That's it. Hold on.

00:40:51.067 --> 00:40:53.251
Two. [Minwoo exhales]

00:40:53.318 --> 00:40:55.100
Again. One.

00:40:55.167 --> 00:40:56.787
[grunts] Lengthen your spine as you inhale.

00:40:56.854 --> 00:40:58.155
- Draw your ribs in. - (student 1) Gosh!

00:40:58.222 --> 00:41:00.382
You should raise your arms. [comical sound] [Minwoo groans]

00:41:00.449 --> 00:41:01.893
You have no strength at all. [smacks]

00:41:01.960 --> 00:41:03.227
My goodness. [students scoff]

00:41:03.740 --> 00:41:05.316
Two...

00:41:05.699 --> 00:41:07.732
- (Mimi) Minwoo, please get up. - (Minwoo) Okay.

00:41:08.502 --> 00:41:10.771
[Minwoo pants] (Mimi) Last one.

00:41:10.838 --> 00:41:12.700
One. [Minwoo grunts]

00:41:14.100 --> 00:41:15.801
[music stops] [faint dog barking]

00:41:15.868 --> 00:41:17.200
[insects chirping]

00:41:17.981 --> 00:41:19.789
[chattering]

00:41:24.167 --> 00:41:25.490
[students laugh]

00:41:28.462 --> 00:41:30.721
(student 1) Minwoo!

00:41:30.788 --> 00:41:32.089
- Come on. - (Minwoo) What? [students laugh]

00:41:32.156 --> 00:41:34.821
[intriguing music] - Let's go. - (Minwoo) Where?

00:41:34.888 --> 00:41:35.818
(student 2) Why, of course,

00:41:35.885 --> 00:41:37.885
We have to throw a welcome party for you.

00:41:37.952 --> 00:41:39.196
[Minwoo laughs awkwardly] No, it's fine.

00:41:39.263 --> 00:41:41.734
- (student 3) Let's go. - (Minwoo) Wait... [chattering]

00:41:42.633 --> 00:41:43.987
- (student 1) What do you want to eat? - (Mimi) Bye.

00:41:44.054 --> 00:41:46.929
- (student 3) Let's have meat. - (Minwoo) Aren't you joining us?

00:41:53.434 --> 00:41:54.915
[fire crackling] [music stops]

00:41:54.982 --> 00:41:56.703
[people chattering]

00:42:03.021 --> 00:42:04.360
(Hagi) Ms. Nam, I'll take that.

00:42:04.427 --> 00:42:05.701
(Dareum) Thank you.

00:42:08.167 --> 00:42:09.648
(Eunjeong) Where did Mija go?

00:42:09.715 --> 00:42:12.215
Tell everyone to come and eat.

00:42:12.282 --> 00:42:13.631
(Dareum) Okay.

00:42:20.224 --> 00:42:21.780
[insects chirping] [footsteps approaching]

00:42:25.560 --> 00:42:26.611
Mom.

00:42:45.133 --> 00:42:47.298
Thanks for helping.

00:42:48.066 --> 00:42:49.169
[Mija sighs]

00:42:49.236 --> 00:42:50.901
I worked so hard to raise you...

00:42:54.441 --> 00:42:58.276
What on earth do you do at that company to work here like this?

00:43:02.391 --> 00:43:05.032
To tell you the truth, Mom...

00:43:06.031 --> 00:43:07.952
(Dareum) there's something I didn't tell you.

00:43:10.724 --> 00:43:11.689
I...

00:43:14.127 --> 00:43:15.393
[exhales]

00:43:15.891 --> 00:43:17.533
I quit...

00:43:17.600 --> 00:43:18.596
SE Trading.

00:43:20.908 --> 00:43:21.899
I know.

00:43:24.936 --> 00:43:25.764
You know?

00:43:25.831 --> 00:43:28.834
I saw your business card that said APPELLO or something.

00:43:30.632 --> 00:43:31.824
[sighs]

00:43:35.814 --> 00:43:37.815
(Dareum) I'm sorry I lied to you.

00:43:39.401 --> 00:43:42.856
You seemed so happy that I was working for SE,

00:43:42.923 --> 00:43:44.889
And I didn't want to disappoint you.

00:43:45.623 --> 00:43:49.748
I'm not sad that you quit a big company.

00:43:53.218 --> 00:43:54.899
I'm sad that you didn't tell me

00:43:56.053 --> 00:43:57.268
(Mija) what was going on.

00:43:58.158 --> 00:43:59.745
[soft music]

00:44:00.767 --> 00:44:02.375
Even when you were in school,

00:44:02.442 --> 00:44:06.167
I wish you'd told me if you were having a hard time.

00:44:07.078 --> 00:44:08.801
I know it was because you didn't want me to worry,

00:44:09.467 --> 00:44:10.775
[inhales]

00:44:11.235 --> 00:44:13.868
But sometimes I wonder if you can't trust me.

00:44:15.834 --> 00:44:18.400
Whenever you hide things from me,

00:44:21.135 --> 00:44:22.527
I feel so upset.

00:44:33.407 --> 00:44:34.467
(Dareum) I'm sorry.

00:44:36.210 --> 00:44:37.408
I won't do that anymore.

00:44:40.180 --> 00:44:41.379
[Dareum sniffles]

00:44:42.850 --> 00:44:43.868
But Mom.

00:44:44.418 --> 00:44:46.384
Even if it's a small company,

00:44:46.840 --> 00:44:48.690
My ideas can be reflected

00:44:48.757 --> 00:44:50.788
And I can have my voice heard.

00:44:52.019 --> 00:44:53.024
I...

00:44:54.382 --> 00:44:55.661
[faint laugh]

00:44:55.728 --> 00:44:58.462
Feel like I'm useful there.

00:44:59.099 --> 00:45:01.299
That's why I like APPELLO,

00:45:03.531 --> 00:45:05.200
And I'm happier here.

00:45:10.599 --> 00:45:11.642
[sniffles]

00:45:14.244 --> 00:45:15.346
(Mija) Then that's fine.

00:45:16.364 --> 00:45:17.682
Wherever you work,

00:45:18.146 --> 00:45:19.383
All I want...

00:45:21.789 --> 00:45:22.954
Is for you to be happy.

00:45:35.002 --> 00:45:36.000
[sniffles]

00:45:37.068 --> 00:45:38.636
Thanks, Mom.

00:45:38.703 --> 00:45:40.838
[sniffles] [pats]

00:45:41.823 --> 00:45:43.133
[exhales]

00:45:49.616 --> 00:45:50.834
[Dareum laughs] (Mija) Gosh.

00:45:51.818 --> 00:45:53.501
[Dareum grunts] [Mija laughs]

00:45:55.978 --> 00:45:57.332
[music stops]

00:45:58.101 --> 00:45:59.231
[sniffles]

00:46:00.937 --> 00:46:02.381
[boiling]

00:46:03.929 --> 00:46:05.529
[people chattering]

00:46:08.376 --> 00:46:10.234
- (Dareum) I should get more meat. - (Mija) Okay.

00:46:12.979 --> 00:46:15.039
Ma'am, try some of this.

00:46:16.176 --> 00:46:17.308
And this too.

00:46:18.111 --> 00:46:19.210
Oh, sure...

00:46:22.636 --> 00:46:23.601
[Hagi grunts]

00:46:24.142 --> 00:46:25.349
(Mija) Please

00:46:25.986 --> 00:46:28.052
Take good care of Dareum. [pouring]

00:46:28.119 --> 00:46:30.105
She's new to the workplace,

00:46:30.172 --> 00:46:31.858
So I'm sure she has a lot to learn. [thuds]

00:46:31.925 --> 00:46:33.591
Well, not a lot.

00:46:34.461 --> 00:46:35.868
Just...

00:46:36.487 --> 00:46:37.504
A little bit.

00:46:37.571 --> 00:46:38.846
[intriguing music]

00:46:38.913 --> 00:46:41.375
But I'm sure she's very hardworking.

00:46:41.442 --> 00:46:43.403
All our employees are hardworking.

00:46:43.470 --> 00:46:44.790
(Mija) I see...

00:46:44.857 --> 00:46:46.222
[laughs]

00:46:46.289 --> 00:46:47.798
[inhales]

00:46:47.865 --> 00:46:49.779
I guess there isn't much to compliment

00:46:50.192 --> 00:46:52.167
About Dareum, then.

00:46:54.234 --> 00:46:56.016
[sips] [music stops]

00:46:56.083 --> 00:46:57.181
Ms. Nam

00:46:58.303 --> 00:46:59.717
Is already a great employee.

00:47:01.129 --> 00:47:02.099
[warm music]

00:47:02.166 --> 00:47:03.423
She's always full of energy

00:47:04.007 --> 00:47:05.701
And does her best,

00:47:05.768 --> 00:47:07.700
(Hagi) so even if she's only recently joined us,

00:47:07.767 --> 00:47:09.400
She's been a great help so far.

00:47:10.464 --> 00:47:11.968
There's no need to worry, ma'am.

00:47:13.667 --> 00:47:15.833
Is that so?

00:47:17.451 --> 00:47:20.738
I did think Ms. Nam was very warmhearted.

00:47:21.381 --> 00:47:23.941
(Hagi) I guess she takes after you.

00:47:24.838 --> 00:47:26.274
(Mija) Oh, my! [laughs]

00:47:26.341 --> 00:47:27.667
[Hagi laughs] My goodness.

00:47:28.415 --> 00:47:29.680
How did you know?

00:47:30.450 --> 00:47:31.467
To be honest,

00:47:31.534 --> 00:47:34.385
Everyone who sees us says she takes after me.

00:47:34.452 --> 00:47:35.655
[laughs] Really? [Mija laughs]

00:47:35.722 --> 00:47:37.267
- (Mija) Let's clink glasses. - (Hagi) Sure.

00:47:38.616 --> 00:47:40.334
[clinks] [Mija laughs]

00:47:44.762 --> 00:47:45.829
(Mija) Wow... [Hagi exclaims]

00:47:45.896 --> 00:47:48.754
You really know how to drink.

00:47:48.821 --> 00:47:49.933
[Hagi reacts]

00:47:50.000 --> 00:47:51.569
- Have another glass. - (Hagi) Sure.

00:47:53.437 --> 00:47:55.106
[pouring] [Mija laughs]

00:47:55.940 --> 00:47:57.675
[Mija exclaims] [Hagi grunts]

00:47:57.742 --> 00:47:59.843
- Let me pour you some too. - (Mija) Okay.

00:47:59.910 --> 00:48:01.200
[pouring] [Mija laughs]

00:48:01.267 --> 00:48:02.200
[music fades]

00:48:02.267 --> 00:48:03.514
By the way... [thuds]

00:48:03.581 --> 00:48:04.900
Is Dareum...

00:48:04.967 --> 00:48:07.184
Seeing anyone at work?

00:48:07.251 --> 00:48:09.122
[ding sound] [intriguing music]

00:48:09.189 --> 00:48:10.433
Or does she seem to like anyone?

00:48:10.500 --> 00:48:11.300
[ding sound]

00:48:11.367 --> 00:48:12.790
(Hagi) Excuse me? [comical sound]

00:48:13.457 --> 00:48:16.597
Well, I'm not sure about that...

00:48:16.664 --> 00:48:17.701
[sighs]

00:48:18.300 --> 00:48:19.430
I'm worried

00:48:19.864 --> 00:48:21.936
Since she doesn't seem interested in dating at all.

00:48:22.003 --> 00:48:23.467
[Hagi exhales] [Mija grunts]

00:48:24.068 --> 00:48:25.069
[Hagi clears throat]

00:48:25.972 --> 00:48:26.968
But...

00:48:27.434 --> 00:48:29.874
(Mija) you look so young.

00:48:30.267 --> 00:48:31.509
[Hagi grunts] (Mija) By any chance,

00:48:32.176 --> 00:48:34.011
Are you single?

00:48:34.678 --> 00:48:37.489
Yes, I am.

00:48:37.556 --> 00:48:38.682
(Mija) Oh!

00:48:39.336 --> 00:48:40.587
Really?

00:48:40.654 --> 00:48:42.253
[inhales] [swish sound]

00:48:42.856 --> 00:48:44.066
Then...

00:48:44.133 --> 00:48:47.901
What's your ideal type?

00:48:48.607 --> 00:48:49.949
- (Hagi) Excuse me? - (Mija) I mean,

00:48:50.016 --> 00:48:52.530
You said Dareum is warmhearted.

00:48:53.063 --> 00:48:56.367
Do you not like women like her? [music fades]

00:48:56.434 --> 00:48:58.896
It's not that... [footsteps approaching]

00:48:58.963 --> 00:49:00.754
[thuds] (Dareum) Mom!

00:49:00.821 --> 00:49:01.828
Jeez...

00:49:01.895 --> 00:49:03.615
Don't say stuff like that.

00:49:03.682 --> 00:49:05.617
Don't ask Mr. Kang such weird questions.

00:49:05.684 --> 00:49:09.831
(Mija) I was just asking him his ideal type out of curiosity.

00:49:09.898 --> 00:49:11.915
(Dareum) You're not supposed to ask questions like that at work.

00:49:11.982 --> 00:49:14.067
- (Mija) Is that so? - And there's a reason why you shouldn't.

00:49:14.134 --> 00:49:17.154
(Mija) Then will you get fired again when you just joined them?

00:49:17.221 --> 00:49:18.789
[Dareum gasps] No way.

00:49:18.856 --> 00:49:19.901
(Mija) What do I do? [sad music]

00:49:19.968 --> 00:49:21.107
(Hagi) Ma'am...

00:49:21.803 --> 00:49:23.434
The man your daughter likes...

00:49:24.795 --> 00:49:25.847
Is actually me.

00:49:27.264 --> 00:49:28.868
[street sounds] [music fades]

00:49:34.601 --> 00:49:36.874
[elevator doors closing]

00:49:38.047 --> 00:49:38.767
[button clicks]

00:49:38.834 --> 00:49:39.901
(Miyeong) Director.

00:49:40.383 --> 00:49:41.632
(employees) Hello.

00:49:41.699 --> 00:49:42.780
Hello.

00:49:43.567 --> 00:49:45.426
(Miyeong) What brings you here?

00:49:45.493 --> 00:49:47.218
(Lee Chan) I'm just dropping by after my shoot.

00:49:47.806 --> 00:49:50.090
Is the marketing team busy these days? [doors close]

00:49:50.157 --> 00:49:52.797
[Miyeong sighs] We're working late every day

00:49:52.864 --> 00:49:54.534
Because of the K-Wave project. [Miyeong laughs]

00:49:58.131 --> 00:49:59.501
(Lee Chan) Hagi hasn't gone home yet, right?

00:50:00.119 --> 00:50:01.599
(Miyeong) He's on a business trip.

00:50:04.800 --> 00:50:05.769
With Ms. Nam.

00:50:07.086 --> 00:50:08.339
- With Ms. Nam? - (Miyeong) Yes.

00:50:09.176 --> 00:50:11.809
To bring in a knot artisan from Ms. Nam's hometown.

00:50:12.379 --> 00:50:14.713
I don't think it's going well,

00:50:14.780 --> 00:50:16.981
But they seem like they won't return until they succeed.

00:50:19.263 --> 00:50:20.614
(Wontae) We're ready for the meeting.

00:50:20.681 --> 00:50:21.886
- (Miyeong) Okay. - (Yeongwoo) Yes.

00:50:22.928 --> 00:50:25.400
(Miyeong) Director, we have to start our meeting now.

00:50:25.467 --> 00:50:26.534
What about you?

00:50:26.601 --> 00:50:27.858
(Lee Chan) Well...

00:50:29.129 --> 00:50:31.493
There's no one to see here, so I should get going.

00:50:31.560 --> 00:50:32.800
(Miyeong) Get home safely, then.

00:50:32.867 --> 00:50:33.934
(Lee Chan) Bye.

00:50:35.467 --> 00:50:37.001
[footsteps fading]

00:50:54.909 --> 00:50:56.409
(Nam Dareum)

00:50:56.433 --> 00:50:59.133
(Event venue map Event introduction lines)

00:51:01.757 --> 00:51:03.957
(K-Wave project APPELLO will win first place!)

00:51:04.134 --> 00:51:05.336
[laughs]

00:51:05.966 --> 00:51:07.499
[whoosh sound]

00:51:08.112 --> 00:51:09.667
[ominous music]

00:51:19.580 --> 00:51:21.414
(Lee Chan) My fan drew this character,

00:51:21.481 --> 00:51:23.100
And it was so cute I memorized it.

00:51:28.886 --> 00:51:30.038
[car beeps]

00:51:38.244 --> 00:51:39.617
[whoosh sound]

00:51:45.601 --> 00:51:46.771
It was Dareum.

00:51:46.838 --> 00:51:48.234
[music stops]

00:51:50.572 --> 00:51:52.682
(Dareum) Are you sure you're not coming with us? [insects chirping]

00:51:52.749 --> 00:51:55.045
You're here for work.

00:51:55.652 --> 00:51:58.081
(Mija) Do your best and convince Ms. Im,

00:51:58.148 --> 00:51:59.901
- okay? - All right.

00:51:59.968 --> 00:52:01.084
Get home safely, Mom.

00:52:01.151 --> 00:52:02.011
(Mija) Okay.

00:52:02.078 --> 00:52:03.754
(Hagi) Get back safely, ma'am.

00:52:04.214 --> 00:52:06.080
Yes, Mr. Kang.

00:52:06.147 --> 00:52:08.058
(Mija) Take good care of my daughter.

00:52:08.125 --> 00:52:09.297
Gosh... [Hagi laughs]

00:52:09.364 --> 00:52:10.156
(Mija) Bye, Eunjeong.

00:52:10.223 --> 00:52:11.665
- (Eunjeong) Bye. - (Mija) Bye.

00:52:11.732 --> 00:52:12.968
- (Dareum) Bye. - (Mija) Yeah.

00:52:14.067 --> 00:52:15.667
- (Dareum) Get home safe. - (Mija) Yeah.

00:52:20.204 --> 00:52:21.733
[insects chirping]

00:52:23.084 --> 00:52:24.811
[clattering] [bright music]

00:52:24.878 --> 00:52:28.200
(Eunjeong) It's nice to hear that you want to try learning this craft.

00:52:28.782 --> 00:52:31.418
But it's difficult even for me when I've been learning for over ten years.

00:52:31.485 --> 00:52:33.584
Ms. Im always says,

00:52:33.651 --> 00:52:35.853
"Making knots is a form of spiritual practice."

00:52:36.590 --> 00:52:39.089
She's been doing it her whole life, but she says it's still difficult.

00:52:39.793 --> 00:52:42.322
Compared to her, I'm still taking baby steps.

00:52:42.389 --> 00:52:43.400
[laughs]

00:52:43.467 --> 00:52:45.500
I haven't even been born yet. [Eunjeong, Dareum laugh]

00:52:45.567 --> 00:52:46.496
Anyway,

00:52:46.563 --> 00:52:48.306
As you can see,

00:52:48.373 --> 00:52:51.872
This cord made by braiding several strands of thread is called "ggeunmok."

00:52:51.939 --> 00:52:54.467
And we're going to make decorative knots with this ggeunmok.

00:52:55.098 --> 00:52:57.913
Then why don't you try it to get a feel for what it's like?

00:52:57.980 --> 00:53:01.100
Let's sit over there.

00:53:02.212 --> 00:53:04.667
I'll tell you the easiest one first.

00:53:05.416 --> 00:53:07.133
This is one of the most basic knots,

00:53:07.200 --> 00:53:09.261
Called the "dongsimgyeol knot."

00:53:09.328 --> 00:53:10.600
- "Dongsimgyeol." - (Hagi) "Dongsimgyeol."

00:53:10.667 --> 00:53:12.956
(Eunjeong) We're going to make a "ko."

00:53:13.023 --> 00:53:14.257
The ko

00:53:14.324 --> 00:53:16.627
- is this round hole here. - Right. The ko.

00:53:16.694 --> 00:53:18.996
(Eunjeong) Take these two strands down here

00:53:19.063 --> 00:53:22.165
And fold them through the second and third ko.

00:53:22.232 --> 00:53:24.582
- Like this? - (Eunjeong) Wow! Great job.

00:53:24.649 --> 00:53:26.102
- Good. - (Dareum) Okay. [music stops]

00:53:30.644 --> 00:53:31.967
[Dareum mutters]

00:53:33.477 --> 00:53:34.867
(Dareum) Fold this...

00:53:35.467 --> 00:53:36.980
And put this up here...

00:53:37.448 --> 00:53:38.795
Do I fold...

00:53:38.862 --> 00:53:41.234
Do I fold this one? Or this one?

00:53:42.745 --> 00:53:44.221
This...

00:53:44.786 --> 00:53:46.990
- (Hagi) It's not that. - (Dareum) What?

00:53:49.475 --> 00:53:51.043
Oh... [lively music]

00:53:51.110 --> 00:53:52.496
- (Hagi) It's not this. - (Dareum) Okay.

00:53:52.563 --> 00:53:54.936
- (Hagi) Put this under this one. - (Dareum) Oh, I see.

00:53:55.003 --> 00:53:57.100
- This one first. - (Hagi) Yes, and then...

00:53:57.167 --> 00:53:59.372
- (Dareum) Okay. - (Hagi) Place it through here.

00:53:59.439 --> 00:54:01.233
- (Dareum) Oh, this one. - (Hagi) Right here...

00:54:01.300 --> 00:54:02.390
- (Dareum) Here... - (Hagi) Yes.

00:54:02.457 --> 00:54:04.300
- (Dareum) Here. Okay. - (Hagi) Yes.

00:54:04.367 --> 00:54:05.645
(Dareum) Got it.

00:54:05.712 --> 00:54:07.177
- (Hagi) That's right. - (Dareum) Like this?

00:54:33.841 --> 00:54:35.587
[music stops] [insects chirping]

00:54:51.301 --> 00:54:52.489
[faint laugh]

00:54:57.064 --> 00:54:59.767
(Dareum) All done!

00:55:00.813 --> 00:55:03.934
Making this in person

00:55:04.630 --> 00:55:07.449
Makes it seem even prettier. I feel so proud.

00:55:09.099 --> 00:55:10.192
(Hagi) You're right.

00:55:10.259 --> 00:55:11.611
[Dareum smacks lips] [inhales]

00:55:11.678 --> 00:55:13.434
I can understand how they say

00:55:13.947 --> 00:55:15.712
It contains time.

00:55:18.241 --> 00:55:19.667
(Hagi) I didn't know

00:55:19.734 --> 00:55:21.761
Even such a small knot took so much work.

00:55:21.828 --> 00:55:22.753
(Dareum) Right.

00:55:26.838 --> 00:55:28.726
[crashing]

00:55:34.070 --> 00:55:35.499
[clattering]

00:55:40.107 --> 00:55:41.572
I was going to clean it myself.

00:55:42.063 --> 00:55:43.707
- Thank you. - It's nothing.

00:55:44.281 --> 00:55:45.272
(Hagi) It's fine.

00:55:45.339 --> 00:55:46.746
Let us know if we can help with anything.

00:55:46.813 --> 00:55:47.801
(Eunjeong) Gosh.

00:55:48.834 --> 00:55:51.548
All my friends who used to learn here are gone now.

00:55:52.109 --> 00:55:54.968
I'm the only official successor left.

00:55:55.614 --> 00:55:57.554
[sighs] So if I don't do this,

00:55:58.509 --> 00:55:59.934
This craft will be gone for good.

00:56:07.086 --> 00:56:08.308
Please,

00:56:08.375 --> 00:56:10.701
Convince Ms. Im.

00:56:13.946 --> 00:56:16.701
(Eunjeong) At this rate, it's only a matter of time

00:56:16.768 --> 00:56:18.075
Before Korean knot-making dies out.

00:56:19.094 --> 00:56:20.915
The work is demanding,

00:56:20.982 --> 00:56:22.079
And making a living with it is difficult.

00:56:23.016 --> 00:56:24.081
Who would want to do this?

00:56:25.655 --> 00:56:27.651
So whether they make it at a factory or anywhere else,

00:56:27.718 --> 00:56:30.490
I just want to show the world that Korean knot-making exists.

00:56:30.557 --> 00:56:31.755
[door opens]

00:56:36.763 --> 00:56:39.067
(Cheongrim) Is this what you've been making knots for all this time?

00:56:39.557 --> 00:56:40.872
Ms. Im...

00:56:42.104 --> 00:56:43.634
If that's how you're going to do this, then leave.

00:56:44.799 --> 00:56:47.404
(Cheongrim) Go and produce them at a factory and earn lots of money!

00:56:48.442 --> 00:56:50.274
[lonely music] Earn money?

00:56:52.137 --> 00:56:55.567
(Eunjeong) If that's really what I wanted, I would've quit already.

00:56:56.635 --> 00:56:58.015
I'm doing this...

00:56:58.082 --> 00:56:59.883
Because I want to protect it.

00:57:00.621 --> 00:57:02.319
Someone has to keep holding onto it!

00:57:02.890 --> 00:57:04.154
I should do what I can...

00:57:06.326 --> 00:57:07.634
But why do you say...

00:57:08.192 --> 00:57:09.960
That it's wrong,

00:57:10.631 --> 00:57:12.396
Just because my way of protecting it is different?

00:57:13.244 --> 00:57:14.631
[Eunjeong sniffles]

00:57:18.456 --> 00:57:19.536
[door opens]

00:57:29.067 --> 00:57:30.601
[Dareum sighs] [door opens]

00:57:33.388 --> 00:57:34.734
[Dareum grunts] [music fades]

00:57:46.600 --> 00:57:47.601
(Hagi) Ms. Nam.

00:57:48.502 --> 00:57:50.000
Yes?

00:57:50.636 --> 00:57:52.205
(Hagi) Will you... [insects chirping]

00:57:52.272 --> 00:57:53.236
Come outside for a bit?

00:57:53.974 --> 00:57:54.871
(Dareum) Oh...

00:57:55.360 --> 00:57:56.406
Hang on.

00:57:56.940 --> 00:57:58.868
[fire crackling] [night bird calling]

00:58:05.901 --> 00:58:07.150
(Hagi) I put this here earlier,

00:58:07.750 --> 00:58:08.846
But I felt bad about eating it alone.

00:58:08.913 --> 00:58:10.501
(Dareum) Sweet potatoes...

00:58:11.758 --> 00:58:13.857
[laughs] You know how to do stuff like this too?

00:58:14.567 --> 00:58:15.599
[Dareum gasps]

00:58:21.293 --> 00:58:23.066
(Hagi) Try it. [Dareum exclaims]

00:58:23.466 --> 00:58:24.968
[gasps] [sniffs]

00:58:25.035 --> 00:58:26.339
The smell is insane.

00:58:26.406 --> 00:58:27.571
Be careful, it's hot.

00:58:28.805 --> 00:58:30.302
[coughs] [bright music]

00:58:30.369 --> 00:58:31.834
[Dareum exclaims] [Dareum pants]

00:58:31.901 --> 00:58:32.979
(Hagi) Ms. Nam, are you okay?

00:58:33.046 --> 00:58:34.711
[Dareum exclaims] [taps feet]

00:58:35.254 --> 00:58:36.118
Just spit it out on my hand.

00:58:36.185 --> 00:58:37.269
[gasps]

00:58:39.783 --> 00:58:42.801
(Dareum) What? He's giving me his hand? [grunts]

00:58:43.461 --> 00:58:45.100
No, it's fine.

00:58:46.200 --> 00:58:47.500
[gulps]

00:58:47.567 --> 00:58:48.925
[grunts] [laughs awkwardly]

00:58:58.389 --> 00:59:00.173
Be careful not to burn yourself.

00:59:00.240 --> 00:59:01.934
[laughs awkwardly] Thank you.

00:59:13.149 --> 00:59:14.333
(Dareum) Why...

00:59:14.400 --> 00:59:17.154
Is he being so nice to me?

00:59:19.089 --> 00:59:20.724
[night bird calling] [fire crackling]

00:59:21.868 --> 00:59:23.267
[music stops] [Dareum grunts]

00:59:24.932 --> 00:59:26.363
(Dareum) This reminds me of my grandma.

00:59:27.837 --> 00:59:30.867
She used to roast sweet potatoes for me when I was little.

00:59:35.375 --> 00:59:36.667
You're lucky.

00:59:38.325 --> 00:59:40.347
(Hagi) You have a loving grandmother...

00:59:40.414 --> 00:59:41.277
[Dareum laughs]

00:59:41.344 --> 00:59:42.649
And a mother.

00:59:42.716 --> 00:59:43.747
[Dareum reacts]

00:59:45.730 --> 00:59:46.801
Thanks to you,

00:59:47.712 --> 00:59:49.170
I had a great time today.

00:59:49.237 --> 00:59:50.200
[Dareum laughs]

00:59:50.267 --> 00:59:51.467
(Dareum) What do you mean?

00:59:52.426 --> 00:59:53.758
[inhales]

00:59:55.662 --> 00:59:57.467
I got to have drinks with your mother.

00:59:58.928 --> 01:00:00.571
[emotional music]

01:00:03.300 --> 01:00:04.935
My mother passed away when I was in high school,

01:00:07.541 --> 01:00:08.939
So I never got to drink with her.

01:00:18.719 --> 01:00:19.816
[laughs]

01:00:22.278 --> 01:00:25.122
Then I guess you crossed an item off your bucket list today.

01:00:27.325 --> 01:00:28.391
I guess so.

01:00:29.269 --> 01:00:30.227
[laughs]

01:00:31.609 --> 01:00:32.662
(Hagi) What about you, Ms. Nam?

01:00:33.388 --> 01:00:34.598
Do you have a bucket list?

01:00:36.266 --> 01:00:38.400
(Dareum) Well... [laughs awkwardly]

01:00:39.206 --> 01:00:42.139
[inhales] Watch a concert in the front row?

01:00:43.734 --> 01:00:45.067
And raise a pet.

01:00:45.612 --> 01:00:46.534
And...

01:00:47.618 --> 01:00:48.745
Hear the words,

01:00:49.759 --> 01:00:51.901
"I'm so glad I have you"

01:00:51.968 --> 01:00:53.934
From someone.

01:00:59.589 --> 01:01:00.906
Well... [laughs awkwardly]

01:01:00.973 --> 01:01:02.634
I guess that's kind of cheesy.

01:01:26.737 --> 01:01:28.752
(Hagi) Oh... [Hagi clears throat]

01:01:30.586 --> 01:01:32.867
I guess I've been sitting too long in front of the fire. [Dareum laughs awkwardly]

01:01:32.934 --> 01:01:34.400
It's hot.

01:01:35.940 --> 01:01:37.801
- I'm going to walk for a bit. - (Dareum) Okay.

01:01:39.112 --> 01:01:40.571
[music stops]

01:01:46.068 --> 01:01:47.100
What about you?

01:01:49.334 --> 01:01:50.340
Do you want...

01:01:51.333 --> 01:01:52.309
To walk with me?

01:01:56.179 --> 01:01:58.097
[wind blowing] [insects chirping]

01:02:01.822 --> 01:02:02.868
(Hagi) I feel like...

01:02:04.819 --> 01:02:06.389
I'll remember this day for a long time.

01:02:08.278 --> 01:02:09.326
(Dareum) Me too.

01:02:10.911 --> 01:02:12.295
I'm really glad

01:02:14.690 --> 01:02:15.899
That I have you, Ms. Nam.

01:02:16.637 --> 01:02:18.034
[lively music]

01:02:19.240 --> 01:02:21.037
[laughs awkwardly]

01:02:21.104 --> 01:02:23.707
My bucket list.

01:02:33.420 --> 01:02:34.400
Ms. Nam.

01:02:36.823 --> 01:02:38.421
(Hagi) You told me once

01:02:39.323 --> 01:02:40.601
That you joined APPELLO

01:02:42.362 --> 01:02:44.200
Because there was someone you wanted to meet.

01:02:44.267 --> 01:02:45.434
[music stops]

01:02:46.661 --> 01:02:48.698
[laughs awkwardly] Well, yeah.

01:02:49.336 --> 01:02:50.500
(Dareum) I did.

01:02:51.495 --> 01:02:52.502
(Dareum) What?

01:02:52.569 --> 01:02:54.300
Why is he suddenly asking that? [intriguing music]

01:02:54.775 --> 01:02:56.373
Be honest with me today.

01:02:58.823 --> 01:03:00.167
(Hagi) That person you wanted to meet...

01:03:01.478 --> 01:03:02.545
Was it me?

01:03:05.708 --> 01:03:06.650
(Dareum) What?

01:03:09.670 --> 01:03:10.954
Do you see me as a man?

01:03:11.992 --> 01:03:12.968
Do you...

01:03:13.660 --> 01:03:15.129
Think...

01:03:15.645 --> 01:03:16.926
I'm...

01:03:16.993 --> 01:03:19.613
Interested in you or something?

01:03:22.119 --> 01:03:23.810
(Hagi) We're alone here right now,

01:03:23.877 --> 01:03:25.501
- so you can be honest... - Wait!

01:03:26.373 --> 01:03:27.370
(Dareum) Hang on.

01:03:27.941 --> 01:03:29.467
Is that why

01:03:29.534 --> 01:03:32.279
You were being cold to me and saying stuff about you being a CEO

01:03:32.346 --> 01:03:33.771
And me being an employee?

01:03:38.048 --> 01:03:40.400
That was the reason?

01:03:41.286 --> 01:03:42.561
[Dareum exhales]

01:03:43.887 --> 01:03:46.393
Well, yes. I know

01:03:46.460 --> 01:03:50.133
Something like that can't happen between the two of us.

01:03:51.033 --> 01:03:53.463
I clearly know who you like.

01:03:55.105 --> 01:03:56.269
[music stops]

01:03:56.336 --> 01:03:57.367
You know what?

01:03:59.701 --> 01:04:00.761
[grunts]

01:04:00.828 --> 01:04:01.801
Who's that?

01:04:02.587 --> 01:04:03.606
[Dareum exclaims]

01:04:04.466 --> 01:04:06.810
Well...

01:04:07.482 --> 01:04:09.111
[sad music]

01:04:12.256 --> 01:04:13.701
Who do I like?

01:04:16.933 --> 01:04:18.100
[Dareum gasps]

01:04:20.861 --> 01:04:22.000
[sighs]

01:04:22.708 --> 01:04:24.861
You like Director Lee Chan!

01:04:25.306 --> 01:04:26.896
- (Hagi) What? - (Dareum) You've liked him

01:04:26.963 --> 01:04:28.431
For a long time!

01:04:29.870 --> 01:04:30.900
[sighs]

01:04:31.438 --> 01:04:32.400
(Hagi) What...

01:04:33.236 --> 01:04:34.638
What did you say?

01:04:34.705 --> 01:04:36.251
But don't worry.

01:04:36.318 --> 01:04:39.754
I swear I'll keep it a secret,

01:04:39.821 --> 01:04:42.145
And I don't have any prejudices at all.

01:04:43.717 --> 01:04:44.781
[scoffs]

01:04:46.086 --> 01:04:48.051
(Hagi) Hang on, Ms. Nam.

01:04:48.956 --> 01:04:50.053
So you mean

01:04:50.762 --> 01:04:51.654
You've been...

01:04:52.175 --> 01:04:54.057
Thinking that I like guys?

01:04:57.883 --> 01:04:59.014
But you do.

01:04:59.081 --> 01:05:00.096
[scoffs]

01:05:00.579 --> 01:05:02.065
[laughs]

01:05:03.152 --> 01:05:04.200
[Hagi laughs] [music stops]

01:05:04.972 --> 01:05:06.000
Ms. Nam.

01:05:06.730 --> 01:05:08.471
I don't like men!

01:05:09.339 --> 01:05:10.707
- (Dareum) What? - (Hagi) And...

01:05:12.579 --> 01:05:14.544
I'm actually interested in a certain woman right now.

01:05:15.395 --> 01:05:17.384
[music: "My Bias, My Boss" theme song]

01:05:17.451 --> 01:05:18.415
(Dareum) What?

01:05:19.000 --> 01:05:21.033
[whoosh sound]

01:05:41.661 --> 01:05:43.192
[light clicks] [music stops]

01:05:44.274 --> 01:05:45.846
[quiet music]

01:05:45.913 --> 01:05:47.000
[door opens]

01:05:48.195 --> 01:05:49.923
[dramatic music]

01:06:24.234 --> 01:06:26.182
[whoosh sound]

01:06:42.062 --> 01:06:43.849
[music stops] [writing sound]

01:06:43.873 --> 01:06:45.573
(Epilogue)

01:06:46.236 --> 01:06:47.534
[playful music]

01:06:48.041 --> 01:06:49.038
[clears throat]

01:06:50.112 --> 01:06:51.133
Should I pull it?

01:06:53.446 --> 01:06:54.934
Oh, yes...

01:06:57.534 --> 01:06:58.534
[Dareum grunts]

01:06:58.901 --> 01:07:00.016
(Dareum) It's done.

01:07:01.788 --> 01:07:02.852
[Dareum laughs awkwardly]

01:07:05.283 --> 01:07:07.136
(Hagi) You get how to do it now, right? [music stops]

01:07:07.203 --> 01:07:08.088
[Dareum reacts]

01:07:08.155 --> 01:07:10.326
Try it again, then.

01:07:12.951 --> 01:07:14.033
[rustles]

01:07:14.401 --> 01:07:15.331
[faint sigh]

01:07:15.398 --> 01:07:16.566
[Dareum laughs]

01:07:16.633 --> 01:07:17.733
(Dareum) Wow...

01:07:17.800 --> 01:07:20.674
This is the first knot I made with you. [rustles]

01:07:20.741 --> 01:07:23.139
Did she say it was called a dongsimgyeol knot?

01:07:23.625 --> 01:07:25.848
[music: "My Bias, My Boss" theme song]

01:07:29.603 --> 01:07:31.147
[Hagi clears throat] [Dareum laughs]

01:07:31.585 --> 01:07:32.782
Why were you startled?

01:07:34.750 --> 01:07:36.085
I wasn't.

01:07:39.899 --> 01:07:41.190
[inhales]

01:07:49.372 --> 01:07:50.790
[whoosh sound]

01:07:53.284 --> 01:07:56.986
(Dongsimgyeol knot "Forever bound together as one") [thud sound]

01:07:57.640 --> 01:07:59.642
(Dareum) Who could he be interested in?

01:08:00.670 --> 01:08:01.744
(Lee Chan) Let's take my car.

01:08:02.203 --> 01:08:03.605
(Hagi) Take my car. [Dareum laughs]

01:08:04.013 --> 01:08:05.766
[Seula, Mimi squeals] (Mimi) What's this turn of events?

01:08:05.833 --> 01:08:07.567
(Minwoo) "That woman I'm interested in is you."

01:08:07.634 --> 01:08:10.256
Why can't you say it? Why can't you?

01:08:10.323 --> 01:08:11.496
(Lee Chan) Why don't we

01:08:11.563 --> 01:08:14.223
Stay by each other's side from now on?

01:08:14.290 --> 01:08:15.018
[knocks] [Dareum gasps]

01:08:15.085 --> 01:08:16.567
[Lee Chan screams] [Dareum gasps]

01:08:16.634 --> 01:08:18.695
(Hagi) Who is she meeting? [people squeal]

01:08:19.796 --> 01:08:21.244
Don't date a guy like that.

01:08:21.311 --> 01:08:22.641
(Dareum) Mr. Kang.

01:08:22.665 --> 01:08:25.665
(Hagi) At least to me, you can say that you're not fine.

